abet letter or silently adding a numerical value.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_alpha_letter_revelation.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"b91cb7cfe48551179c2d25d02abf3d8dc77ee667e9473943c83d46b9132ef2c5":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_anchor_acts","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"y\u00eblyemargl\u00c9z\u00cben","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_anchor_acts","ipa":"","label":"kjv_anchor_acts","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"y\u00fclyemargl\u00e4zhwen","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_anchor_acts","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Anchor,a vessel-holding device in Acts27,ship-hold. Distinguished from a ships internal hold or an abstract source of emotional stability;no unprinted material or design supplied.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_anchor_acts.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"5f8cf8a6986f359610c007697a19a45bff39f91f75f221e6b39fded94ff77947":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_anchor_hope_hebrews","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"y\u00eblyemargl\u00c9z\u00cben","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_anchor_hope_hebrews","ipa":"","label":"kjv_anchor_hope_hebrews","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"y\u00fclyemargl\u00e4zhwen","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_anchor_hope_hebrews","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Anchor of the soul in Hebrews6:19,hope as the holding-device image,sharing ship-hold. Explicit metaphorical extension of the actual nautical anchor;no literal vessel,anchor material or medical emotional-stability diagnosis is asserted.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_anchor_hope_hebrews.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"17c789f5ea3ea974ae2b7c21fe5384fe38ff119b1d47e2224b888b351c2c1773":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_asscolt","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"\u00d3\u00d7bunpelna","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_asscolt","ipa":"","label":"kjv_asscolt","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"th\u0113bunpelna","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_asscolt","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Young offspring of an ass; distinct from the inherited male horse colt.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_asscolt.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"425f86286d64225eb3a8d4f7de4bb9f1a3b37719e3c51ba82949f4144c01fae8":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_assfoal","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"pelna\u00d3\u00d7bun","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_assfoal","ipa":"","label":"kjv_assfoal","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"pelnath\u0113bun","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_assfoal","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Young offspring of an ass, source foal; its sex is not specified.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_assfoal.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"177312969be790833453f413d7d3536f99aee5d4f5f6a2e4fc242b8022160f47":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_aul","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"duldests\u00ebnal","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_aul","ipa":"","label":"kjv_aul","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"duldests\u00fcnal","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_aul","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Aul, the source spelling of the piercing tool used on the servant ear; an awl rather than a weapon or a decorative earring.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_aul.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"02e1deef60e58691b0accaa318817b80de724868328d7e7909af895caadad3ed":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_baptize","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"yemyatprodna","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_baptize","ipa":"","label":"kjv_baptize","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"yemyatprodna","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_baptize","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Baptize:the source ritual washing,water-wash-set-apart. Retains baptism as its named act without specifying an unprinted mode of immersion or sprinkling;Spirit/fire uses remain the source's extensions of this same verb.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_baptize.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"3098e883e4b396f28b53753a8e6d8cdd5267600d2242e002353ff21405ab36cf":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_bay_water","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"goryemslunor","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_bay_water","ipa":"","label":"kjv_bay_water","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"goryemslunor","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_bay_water","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"A bay or inlet of the sea in a boundary description; sea-bend, distinct from the horse colour bay.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_bay_water.sense","status":"draft"}],"statu