 without an unprinted identification with Zebedee's or Alphaeus's son.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_james_judas_brother.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"10d5553b1f032ae637bd56e26881d351c0861b579db5ddfc62ac07b5530d6752":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_japhia_city","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"yafia","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_japhia_city","ipa":"","label":"kjv_japhia_city","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"yafia","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_japhia_city","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Source name city, distinct from earlier king Japhia. Same form, distinct semantic identity.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_japhia_city.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"c978239c664c6c9ec6cdc3ae6eefcc8c42e82d1a78ab93341b499cec5559aae8":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_jasher","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"jeminsevar","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_jasher","ipa":"","label":"kjv_jasher","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"jeminsevar","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_jasher","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Source Jasher: name in the source book citation; no external text imported. Identity follows the supplied local relationship, with no modern place/ethnicity asserted.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_jasher.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"105f212a293527c2ca2cf26f037b9936ff1ce49347bf8fdf564db31119e7f0c7":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_jew","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"yeh\u00e7d\u00c5s\u00dflum","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_jew","ipa":"","label":"kjv_jew","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"yeh\u016bd\u0101s\u014dlum","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_jew","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"A person of the people called Jews in16:6; Judah-person. Preserve the source designation and its opposition to the Syrians without importing a later religious definition or silently substituting another population.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_jew.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"fc7560779b4d7cca66bf09b73098821bd8afd49955dfa76b1c75dbbf53b26839":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_jezreelite","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"yezreels\u00dflum","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_jezreelite","ipa":"","label":"kjv_jezreelite","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"yezreels\u014dlum","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_jezreelite","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Jezreelite, a person identified with Jezreel; place-person, retaining Naboths local designation without an invented ancestry.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_jezreelite.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"df8da2f612e97df8fe76ffecd5f18c6ff9fe48a98f80499455c94da8fa4748de":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_jobab_king","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"yobab","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_jobab_king","ipa":"","label":"kjv_jobab_king","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"yobab","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_jobab_king","