{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_lamb","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"A young sheep, without an inferred sex unless a modifier is supplied.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_lamb.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"36d67f8007644314ec545ee2d6ca1d2b98b06bd01c128534d284aed9b26bdc80":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_latter_rain","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"nabyemsh\u00ebth","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_latter_rain","ipa":"","label":"kjv_latter_rain","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"nabyemsh\u00fcth","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_latter_rain","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Latter rain,the later seasonal rain named in the source comparison,rain-after. Not necessarily rainfall arriving later than expected,and no exact month or modern weather pattern asserted.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_latter_rain.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"2e83738d02bc97c6b8bd09a60441b0c3543af77f592fa18e0a23f5bb93b5b410":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_laver","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"yemyatyems\u00d7borel","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_laver","ipa":"","label":"kjv_laver","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"yemyatyems\u0113borel","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_laver","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"A washing basin or laver used by the sanctuary, distinct from its supporting foot.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_laver.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"b28d3cf12bb6b36a19ceed8b8e1b2e6485e1ee87468b57f74e3cdaea34d7c3c5":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_lick","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"tomilthrendar","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_lick","ipa":"","label":"kjv_lick","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"tomilthrendar","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_lick","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Move the tongue over a surface or take up with the tongue, source ox licking grass and metaphorical consumption by a multitude.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_lick.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"5a4f8c79761b39d4aa8fd6218aed709159c779cee79dda39d2e1e1bce24f18b8":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_lintel","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"dar\u00c5elna","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_lintel","ipa":"","label":"kjv_lintel","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"dar\u0101elna","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_lintel","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"The upper horizontal member of a doorway, named separately from its two side posts.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_lintel.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"158f1e757beaba0fc00c48f266dd98a262b482f3f949374cc40b04d46d1c45dd":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_low_cattle","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"bor\u00c5giktenv\u00d7j\u00cden","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_low_cattle","ipa":"","label":"kjv_low_cattle","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"bor\u0101giktenv\u0113j\u0117ren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_low_cattle","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Make a bovine lowing sound, cow-voice; distinct from low position or rank.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_low_cattle.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"ca2a214a4bc6cb96e903e494494439ffe112e29655d3da6879baaee2a6b73058":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_lunatic_source","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"\u00c5\u00d9b\u00d7rmuren","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_lunatic_source","ipa":"","label":"kjv_lunatic_source","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"adjective","pronunciation":"\u0101ngb\u0113rmuren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_lunatic_source","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Lunatick,the historical lunar-illness label in Matthew4:24. Retains the source category without asserting lunar causation or retrospectively diagnosing epilepsy or a psychiatric condition.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_lunatic_source.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"3890613e122e0c0d6797e037e863c0a0deb4a3d74065a99f0542bd2ad3b1878b":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_mast","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"y\u00eblyemarkoj","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_mast","ipa":"","label":"kjv_mast","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"y\u00fclyemarkoj","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_mast","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Mast,the ship's upright spar,ship-stand;Proverbs23:34places a precarious sleeper at its top. The verse supplies no rigging design,ship class or exact height.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_mast.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"eddd0c1633737b4ec90304bf94e461a9b9a9c738fec2096f9550994e0e4ca141":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_melzar","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"jemoi","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_melzar","ipa":"","label":"kjv_melzar","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"jemoi","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_melzar","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Melzar,the supplied designation of the keeper over Daniel and his three companions;no assertion here about name versus historical title. Supplied local relationship retained without invented etymology, namesake merger or outside harmonization.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_melzar.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"44b6e136af6e8813930fb9ab07dbc8e86c09eec0171a31ce0264b55987b3d1dc":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_mention","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"giktenv\u00d7j\u00cdenden","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_mention","ipa":"","label":"kjv_mention","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"giktenv\u0113j\u0117renden","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_mention","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Make spoken reference to someone or something, voice-name; does not require a formal naming ceremony.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_mention.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"af0b236af62c1cc4d07b5b3d983f4734b73c9ecd3e30e0292deee6e9e47eddcb":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_omega_letter_revelation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"h\u00eb\u00d5\u2019na \u00ddvden","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_omega_letter_revelation","ipa":"","label":"kjv_omega_letter_revelation","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"h\u00fc\u0167h\u2019na \u012bvden","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_omega_letter_revelation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Omega,the supplied Greek-letter name in Revelation's self-designation. Keep it beside ending/last,without replacing it with a local alphabet endpoint or imposing a divine person count.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_omega_letter_revelation.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"ae5ee364b60ee4086cff9ef7ab78933a7bb763291a50f7dfed89f3184676af2d":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_perfume","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"nelverj\u00c9gwa\u00c3l\u00dfn","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_perfume","ipa":"","label":"kjv_perfume","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"nelverj\u00e4gwajzhl\u014dn","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_perfume","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"A prepared fragrant mixture, here sacred incense; not necessarily an alcohol-based liquid fragrance.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_perfume.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"53d48d501f62aeb16900118d00a4437d0610e231c6d0c8f124491817195cc121":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_perfumer","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"nelverj\u00c9gwa\u00c3l\u00dfns\u00dflum","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_perfumer","ipa":"","label":"kjv_perfumer","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"nelverj\u00e4gwajzhl\u014dns\u014dlum","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_perfumer","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Maker or compounder of fragrant preparations, perfume-person; contextual source confectionary, not a sweets-maker. Easton dictionary entry at https://kingjamesbibledictionary.com/Dictionary/confection supports the historical contextual sense.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_perfumer.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"d3f4bb6aed130816d544b7c9fb04c74b4e9e6543a1615cbe9dce1325134e6c39":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_plaster_apply","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"darshal","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_plaster_apply","ipa":"","label":"kjv_plaster_apply","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"darshal","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_plaster_apply","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Apply plaster to a wall or house surface; a verbal conversion of the inherited plaster material.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_plaster_apply.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"79fa267bc8326f5f58732ae9552f03fa59fc357803ce99e141bef00730c495ef":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_porch","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"dar\u00c5el\u00e7l\u00d7on","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_porch","ipa":"","label":"kjv_porch","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"dar\u0101el\u016bl\u0113on","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_porch","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"An entrance-side space or passage, door-place, in the supplied escape account. Does not prescribe a modern architectural plan.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_porch.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"824829883eb5ff1aef7a75ab494fe7229f88220830d51eb28bbc462894f1d034":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_priestly_course","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"prodvard\u00c7vens\u00dflumstrasen","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_priestly_course","ipa":"","label":"kjv_priestly_course","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"prodvard\u00e3vens\u014dlumstrasen","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_priestly_course","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"A priestly service division or course,priest-division,as named for Abia in Luke1. Not a route or a command;its rotation is expressed separately by the inherited service-order term.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_priestly_course.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"fc2d964cff6d57cb56ed773d827f5d8f92572a004f0913674473a25a80e3c6b3":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_pulse_food","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"p\u00e1wemind\u00cdn\u00d7r","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_pulse_food","ipa":"","label":"kjv_pulse_food","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"p\u00f4wemind\u0117rn\u0113r","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_pulse_food","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Pulse as edible legume food, bean-food; distinct from the inherited heartbeat noun.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_pulse_food.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"9472f4b72714e6161ddf2784b19d6cc0ee4195d0cf810bd4454ac29889cc3b2a":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_quicksand_acts","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"melkwesthren","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_quicksand_acts","ipa":"","label":"kjv_quicksand_acts","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"melkwesthren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_quicksand_acts","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Quicksands,the feared unstable sands or sandy shipping hazard in Acts27:17,soft-sand. Preserves the source hazard label without imposing a modern dramatic sinking-pit mechanism or a substituted proper geographic name.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_quicksand_acts.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"f65007dcf220c9c853cbd32ad000339a8c41f41fd3e193ac8dd3f4dd943ab617":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_rabsaris","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"var\u00dfnna z\u00e1l haren","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_rabsaris","ipa":"","label":"kjv_rabsaris","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"var\u014dnna z\u00f4l haren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_rabsaris","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Rabsaris, supplied Assyrian official designation. Local source identity retained without invented etymology or harmonization.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_rabsaris.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"861b14dd4c31ca511e23e4de7c1bf076d68bdc945fdb68360774618480623431":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_rabsaris_babylon","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"var\u00dfnna z\u00e1l haren","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_rabsaris_babylon","ipa":"","label":"kjv_rabsaris_babylon","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"var\u014dnna z\u00f4l haren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_rabsaris_babylon","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Rabsaris,the printed Babylonian official designation inJeremiah39;kept beside named officials without asserting identity with the earlier Assyrian bearer. Supplied local relationship retained without invented etymology, namesake merger or outside harmonization.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_rabsaris_babylon.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"29ed2b7600e926f6752613377425cbc8fbdea40850e435f29bde8f107545cf55":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_rabshakeh","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"tremborel jem\u00e3s\u00dflum haren","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_rabshakeh","ipa":"","label":"kjv_rabshakeh","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"tremborel jemois\u014dlum haren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_rabshakeh","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Rabshakeh, supplied designation of the Assyrian spokesman. Local source identity retained without invented etymology or harmonization.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_rabshakeh.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"a8069e2942379a7834f87c65c7aaa59e03e2d5b152896733a415925beec1c38f":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_rainbow_revelation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"nabyemslunorthiril","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_rainbow_revelation","ipa":"","label":"kjv_rainbow_revelation","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"nabyemslunorthiril","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_rainbow_revelation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Rainbow in Revelation4:3,rain-bow built on the inherited cloud-bow extension. Retain the around-throne and emerald-like appearance without replacing the visionary comparison by a physical optical explanation.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_rainbow_revelation.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"687ab70e8fd8ef4a310c405be8dc988b4b0f59c9afe45d41aa4eca8632c45784":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_rattle","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"zivelj\u00cden","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_rattle","ipa":"","label":"kjv_rattle","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"zivelj\u0117ren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_rattle","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Make repeated small hard shaking sounds,shake-sound;the quiver rattles against the horse. Not a claim about a specific harness construction.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_rattle.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"7b92d5af45d785064a96a52f24707c47536c24760950f7612711f1332d8f8ffe":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_red_sea","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"azgoryems","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_red_sea","ipa":"","label":"kjv_red_sea","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"azgoryems","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_red_sea","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"The named Red sea in this supplied English source; its name is translated as red-sea without substituting a proposed modern geographic identification.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_red_sea.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"459323ecfd48bea0e0839120d8c5174dc35b1fd3ae1d4257b9d8cda28b5efa3e":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_reformation_hebrews","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"hif\u00e5rorp\u00e1f\u00d7a\u00d9","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_reformation_hebrews","ipa":"","label":"kjv_reformation_hebrews","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"hifourorp\u00f4f\u0113ang","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_reformation_hebrews","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Reformation in Hebrews9:10,arrange-renew,the setting-right or renewed arrangement to which the imposed ritual ordinances point. Not the later historical Protestant Reformation,ordinary disciplinary punishment,or the reshaping of a physical object.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_reformation_hebrews.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"cdf24e7e670239f77c5bb3ad8a7d9ac750216dae072cf86710ab1455d94455c4":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_refresh","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"p\u00e1f\u00d7jw\u00ebnenplesten","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_refresh","ipa":"","label":"kjv_refresh","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"p\u00f4f\u0113jw\u00fcnenplesten","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_refresh","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Restore vigour through relief or rest, here humans benefiting from cessation; not merely reload a display or replace an object.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_refresh.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"af1464e8f18b426cd91be047495637dd4bf937f239e694985a4f9b799c1f976a":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_resound","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"j\u00cdensezif\u00c7\u00c3","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_resound","ipa":"","label":"kjv_resound","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"j\u0117rensezif\u00e3jzh","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_resound","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"To resound or ring with a returning sound, sound-return; source rang again does not require a second coronation.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_resound.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"d9c659de282a2d8fcab038b24518a6ad1d1e859d746a7f7899b8c8c7cd5e1614":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_rigging","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"y\u00eblyemarthiril jw\u00ebnenplesten","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_rigging","ipa":"","label":"kjv_rigging","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"y\u00fclyemarthiril jw\u00fcnenplesten","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_rigging","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Tacklings as a vessel's rigging or cordage,ship-cord;Isaiah33:23 distinguishes this from the mast and sail. Does not describe sporting tackles or generic tools.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_rigging.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"e394a7069db1b6dbe933279baa73f7dfc99b67874dc636bc9c18f0508375b65b":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_robe_train","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"thani felenvorh\u00eb\u00d3","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_robe_train","ipa":"","label":"kjv_robe_train","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"thani felenvorh\u00fcth","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_robe_train","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Train of a robe,the trailing garment portion filling the temple in the vision; robe-tail,not teaching,a railway or a retinue.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_robe_train.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"e666e247933172540bd34d63a592a268f953af1d4cd69b29612fad50cb94fd26":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_row","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"goryemskloj","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_row","ipa":"","label":"kjv_row","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"goryemskloj","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_row","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Sea-draw, propel a vessel by pulling oars. Distinct from row, a line of things.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_row.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"d585e642af3a1107f0b38f0821f5eb811e12f0bf6ef7e087601073c6d22ef0f3":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_rudder_acts","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"y\u00eblyemarelyi\u00d1","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_rudder_acts","ipa":"","label":"kjv_rudder_acts","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"y\u00fclyemarelyich","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_rudder_acts","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Rudder,the steering member of the ship in Acts27:40,ship-turn. The source plural bands are expressed separately;no modern single-stern-rudder design is asserted.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_rudder_acts.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"02601262e8e9f7dad4266ef50f5b16e8ae009d6541826c5583c7b49f8538f212":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_sailor","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"goryemsd\u00c7\u00d3s\u00dflum","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_sailor","ipa":"","label":"kjv_sailor","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"goryemsd\u00e3ths\u014dlum","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_sailor","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Sea-worker; a mariner, not the ship's master by default.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_sailor.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"f7b69822ac20c05a591814230622124b0577baa8a0a004dd3d7a60729e7367fb":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_scorpion","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"jerdestkerin\u00d5\u00dfrvor","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_scorpion","ipa":"","label":"kjv_scorpion","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"jerdestkerin\u0167h\u014drvor","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_scorpion","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Scorpion, the source stinging animal in the wilderness list; claw-sting-beast calque without an invented zoological species.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_scorpion.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"4f0f7f895164375cf018e1a5547e4b959ff00ab3aef9f5bf0e7f7427c5279129":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_scroll_leaf","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"\u00ddvelythrenin","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_scroll_leaf","ipa":"","label":"kjv_scroll_leaf","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"\u012bvelythrenin","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_scroll_leaf","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"A written portion or leaf of the roll inJeremiah36:23,scroll-part. Retains the source reading-unit without asserting a modern bound page or a botanical leaf.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_scroll_leaf.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"735ca46a4cf6ce972650196413a84f4f0da9ae49c3677f0682614b5894ff6bee":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_sea_basin","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"goryems","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_sea_basin","ipa":"","label":"kjv_sea_basin","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"goryems","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_sea_basin","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Sea as the name of the large cast basin; shares sea while recording a bounded ritual vessel rather than an ocean.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_sea_basin.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"ad47c4235667f752bf3f9a3761f929cb5e5f30fb918345a6a04f7374dede16bb":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_sea_monster","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"goryemsmar \u00cddema\u00d5\u00dfrna","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_sea_monster","ipa":"","label":"kjv_sea_monster","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"goryemsmar \u0117rdema\u0167h\u014drna","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_sea_monster","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Sea monster,the supplied historical nursing creature label inLamentations4:3. Sea-monster compound preserves the printed category without silently substituting jackal or asserting modern zoological identification.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_sea_monster.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"dc93b36b19f24b8a361bac4a93308373adbd8df45eb330a183e343b5324f77a5":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_seaman","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"goryemss\u00dflum","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_seaman","ipa":"","label":"kjv_seaman","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"goryemss\u014dlum","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_seaman","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"A seafarer or shipman, sea-person; the source explicitly qualifies these attendants by knowledge of the sea.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_seaman.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"c72068cb1c72589851b06575146b23b56cc10825a2164a9fa04652aba608e85c":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_seaweed","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"goryemsverzet","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_seaweed","ipa":"","label":"kjv_seaweed","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"goryemsverzet","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_seaweed","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Sea-plant, the weeds wrapping the drowning speaker's head.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_seaweed.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"b1c18075b2320e9ed9f14598a8a9b280641bafca74ffa42c9a75a496b7d5918c":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_ship_boat_acts","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"viminy\u00eblyemar","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_ship_boat_acts","ipa":"","label":"kjv_ship_boat_acts","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"viminy\u00fclyemar","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_ship_boat_acts","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Boat,the subsidiary craft carried or towed with the main ship in Acts27,small-ship. Distinct from the main vessel and from the earlier river ferry;no exact size,capacity or hull design is added.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_ship_boat_acts.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"343807661f47581fb37e4bf43a62e6db9299c8472f5673743eb65823536ca0ff":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_ship_pilot","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"y\u00eblyemarmiktaz\u00d7rs\u00dflum","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_ship_pilot","ipa":"","label":"kjv_ship_pilot","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"y\u00fclyemarmiktaz\u0113rs\u014dlum","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_ship_pilot","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"A navigator or guiding officer of a ship,ship-guide;source pilot,distinct from the general sailor and from an aircraft pilot.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_ship_pilot.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"2df851d3a1b2189aff725f1cec5ba687d833fe084b855de4d5b4145b38e16e36":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_ship_stern","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"y\u00eblyemarh\u00ebthin","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_ship_stern","ipa":"","label":"kjv_ship_stern","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"y\u00fclyemarh\u00fcthin","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_ship_stern","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"The hinder part or stern of the ship in Mark4:38,ship-behind;distinct from rear meaning upbringing or stern meaning severity. No unprinted boat design is asserted.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_ship_stern.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"6978eb6c18a2f15f83ea2cc0ff3a68cd90e8663f7dfdef1e4c5e7b5abd28b593":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_shipmaster","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"y\u00eblyemarmarven","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_shipmaster","ipa":"","label":"kjv_shipmaster","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"y\u00fclyemarmarven","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_shipmaster","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Ship-master, person commanding the vessel.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_shipmaster.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"563b060595a306206126fae7238d96c9a52f0b3b0754afe62c983bf6a5e24a87":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_shipwreck_corinthians","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"y\u00eblyemarika\u00d9","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_shipwreck_corinthians","ipa":"","label":"kjv_shipwreck_corinthians","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"y\u00fclyemarikang","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_shipwreck_corinthians","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Shipwreck in2Corinthians11:25,ship-breaking or wrecking suffered by the speaker. The three occurrences are retained without identifying them with an unprinted voyage or treating the separately narrated Acts wreck as part of this count.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_shipwreck_corinthians.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"5aa6e932f206f21cce89c3331280cfb6d2150e7fa841ed2d172dbfa3d5f9a867":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_shore","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"goryemsthren","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_shore","ipa":"","label":"kjv_shore","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"goryemsthren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_shore","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"The edge of land adjoining water, sea-edge, not a shore used as a supporting prop.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_shore.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"b39a30e5c87f490798c21bc633dad77af5c3581f049072268be6c37141eb063b":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_soap","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"yemyatvoren","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_soap","ipa":"","label":"kjv_soap","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"yemyatvoren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_soap","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Soap,the cleansing substance paired with nitre,wash-matter. Keeps the supplied historical label distinct from the mineral without asserting a chemical formula or recipe.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_soap.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"b88b25357b8687a7a4c8dd67cdde67f602e0a42c121b3bee1655eac1c5017e60":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_supple_wash","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"yemyatmel","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_supple_wash","ipa":"","label":"kjv_supple_wash","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"yemyatmel","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_supple_wash","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"The supplied infant-washing purpose to supple in Ezekiel16:4,wash-soft. Retains the source's archaic easing/cleansing wording without prescribing a practice or importing an anatomical mechanism.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_supple_wash.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"b4f332f40d2792a5d781c853637b155637c40675a1c355bfaa1f46d6f9c1c042":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_talitha_quoted","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"pelnapelena","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_talitha_quoted","ipa":"","label":"kjv_talitha_quoted","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"particle","pronunciation":"pelnapelena","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_talitha_quoted","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Talitha,the first quoted token of Mark5:41's preserved utterance. Its supplied interpretation follows separately;the token is not an ordinary Vayrshemon lexical girl noun.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_talitha_quoted.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"8bdb3275c4f4f0e5b88cb14d5cafbedc857d94d573b6810c01ff3b913c08681a":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_tartan","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"haren hefak gur","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_tartan","ipa":"","label":"kjv_tartan","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"haren hefak gur","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_tartan","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Tartan, supplied designation of an Assyrian official; no invented personal biography. Local source identity retained without invented etymology or harmonization.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_tartan.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"5b68c1d1c4f012528d2db8ae4df11b8a7ec767970a82988a1be546ab4af24e5d":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_threshold","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"dar\u00c5elpales","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_threshold","ipa":"","label":"kjv_threshold","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"dar\u0101elpales","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_threshold","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"The sill at a doorway, door-foot; the physical place on which the source locates the hands, not an abstract decision boundary.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_threshold.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"710f2db441f3e9f0b680bb5a8c5d91bfa899b78a72ad68945ff1382608e1ed89":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_tinkle","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"zarj\u00cden","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_tinkle","ipa":"","label":"clink","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"zarj\u0117ren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_tinkle","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Make a light repeated ringing sound,metal-sound;the source tinkling of foot ornaments,without asserting a specific bell design.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_tinkle.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"d7e1bc8c80f9321773aea195767a05b6cd343a3bae33aef93b7988a77c21f8a9":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_towel_john","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"yemyatfelen","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_towel_john","ipa":"","label":"kjv_towel_john","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"yemyatfelen","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_towel_john","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Towel in John13,wash-cloth,the cloth with which Jesus girds himself and wipes feet;no modern size,material or distinction between bathing accessories invented.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_towel_john.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"f23eccc299497500a08ed4524b86c5e2fa3c336d7a220795afaf71e10526dd10":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_twilight","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"b\u00d7rvimb\u00d7\u00c7r","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_twilight","ipa":"","label":"kjv_twilight","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"b\u0113rvimb\u0113\u00e3r","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_twilight","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"Twilight, the dim light at a boundary between day and night, dim-light; the source does not supply a clock hour.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_twilight.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"4b2a95cfd74202bd9830491b3a628121a3463f911f085811dc938f3b4248818e":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_twin","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"\u00d5\u00c5tus gura\u00d9\u00d5\u00dfr","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_twin","ipa":"","label":"kjv_twin","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"\u0167h\u0101tus gurang\u0167h\u014dr","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_twin","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"One of two offspring of the same pregnancy; paired-birth person, not merely similar-looking people.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_twin.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"8f80f40a1b9b06667585aebe0e2608a2ffd6d8299ebb423f07fdff265b6e712c":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_washpot","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"yemyatborem","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_washpot","ipa":"","label":"kjv_washpot","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"yemyatborem","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_washpot","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"A pot for washing,wash-pot;Moab is compared to this lowly vessel in divine territorial speech,without inventing its material or a ritual procedure.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_washpot.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"1ba7f4f6b51798315808be16f4d4425520ee4b87bbb17f9753ce07f99ee8aca5":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_waver_limp","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"etymology":"Sealed Bible vocabulary review","exampleIds":[],"headword":"m\u00e5rstrasenna","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_waver_limp","ipa":"","label":"kjv_waver_limp","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"mourstrasenna","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_waver_limp","sourceId":"shakespeare014.bible.0.10-kjv.285"}],"definition":"To waver or hobble between competing positions, walk-divided; source halt between opinions retains bodily instability without asserting diagnosed lameness.","id":"shakespeare014.biblical-vocabulary.kjv_waver_limp.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"74ea80c381d6ed3a457efa0e383360cebab67ccf32749b86770730029e51b2e2":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"lex.kjv_witch"