 person is distinct.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.aaron_tamora_companion.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"0c3b74d59d887a4feff666b20b5bdc28a7e28d33a464bd0b99f4485a1fde271b":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: holy + mother + head","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-comedy-of-errors.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: holy + mother + head","exampleIds":[],"headword":"prodnamelaharen","id":"shakespeare014.lex.abbess_religious_head","ipa":"","label":"abbess_religious_head","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"prodnamelaharen","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-comedy-of-errors.r1"}],"definition":"Head of the priory who offers the visitors sanctuary. The stage uses her office before revealing that she is Emilia.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.abbess_religious_head.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"0377fc4d261c832bd736715274ff5fb89fc602a40d3fc2c444905eea721e8d35":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: cloister + house","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.king-john.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: cloister + house","exampleIds":[],"headword":"prod\u00e1pe\u00dbem\u00e7l\u00d7ono\u00c3t\u00e7z\u00e1l","id":"shakespeare014.lex.abbey_religious_house","ipa":"","label":"abbey_religious_house","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"prod\u00f4peshem\u016bl\u0113onojzht\u016bz\u00f4l","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.king-john.r1"}],"definition":"A religious house under an abbot. John intends to charge these houses with the cost of the expedition.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.abbey_religious_house.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"f65e96089a26ffada0fa1f248a5434617664cc5d50bb70cad76a