nch_lear_hound","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"vesh","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.king-lear.r1"}],"definition":"The white-named dog in Lear's list. Distinct from the Lady Blanche of King John.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.blanch_lear_hound.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"34c20ce29bf1c0c73dca98c26371558a83d5a2db4f36a78eabbc8f866efbce47":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.king-john.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"blan\u00db","id":"shakespeare014.lex.blanche_john_niece","ipa":"","label":"blanche_john_niece","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"blansh","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.king-john.r1"}],"definition":"John's niece, the Lady Blanche of Spain who arrives with Eleanor and is proposed as the Dauphin's bride.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.blanche_john_niece.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"9c3b916fca923746a93ce76377bf68f11736b31bc79abb38de40665b2996d36e":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation/sense: fire + light","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation/sense: fire + light","exampleIds":[],"headword":"zarunb\u00d7\u00c7r","id":"shakespeare014.lex.blaze_flame","ipa":"","label":"blaze_flame","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"zarunb\u0113\u00e3r","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"definition":"A bright burning flame, figuratively the people\u2019s anger in the stubble image; no new literal conflagration is asserted.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.blaze_flame.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"7ab9ae1b30a1f4438a38dec766fa0aab404616a053fe7e1a87a3db196f139912":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Native lexical derivation from blood, flow","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"etymology":"Native lexical derivation from blood, flow","exampleIds":[],"headword":"z\u00e1rren","id":"shakespeare014.lex.bleed","ipa":"","label":"bleed","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"z\u00f4rren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"definition":"Lose flowing blood, literally or in the heart\u2019s sorrow metaphor.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.bleed.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"c8ec539d4e299b54b6be2b1579fac5304cf57817cfee9cd35a2debaa29adce4c":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of fault","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of fault","exampleIds":[],"headword":"murf\u00d7venor","id":"shakespeare014.lex.blemish","ipa":"","label":"blemish","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"murf\u0113venor","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"definition":"A perceived stain or imperfection, including imagined reputational damage; distinct from an asserted bodily defect.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.blemish.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"e16927dd359caebd99786719ca20b2ee4f8c0ed6a23ec801ee1970e2e81ad9e6":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Native lexical derivation from sprout, kill","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"etymology":"Native lexical derivation from sprout, kill","exampleIds":[],"headword":"verzetnevgrij","id":"shakespeare014.lex.blight","ipa":"","label":"blight","notes":"","orthographyI