 the planning function among the body\u2019s faculties.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.devise_plan.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"64891ed9e0b6a985c827dbffc93fff59696a54bb8b4761138575b5dbff3f2ac7":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted geographic-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.richard-iii.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted geographic-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"devon\u00dbir","id":"shakespeare014.lex.devonshire_rising_county","ipa":"","label":"devonshire_rising_county","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"devonshir","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.richard-iii.r1"}],"definition":"County named in the report of Courtney and the Bishop of Exeter taking arms.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.devonshire_rising_county.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"372fcb54291877669e23c024a1f0830057d7dfabee7f0dd58b42f4f94c47af80":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of attend","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of attend","exampleIds":[],"headword":"d\u00c7ven","id":"shakespeare014.lex.devoted_observance","ipa":"","label":"devoted_observance","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"d\u00e3ven","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"definition":"Devoted respectful attendance or service to the beloved. Nominal native attend, with both source occurrences retained; not a calendar observance or the editor\u2019s substituted obedience.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.devoted_observance.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"f30308b51a62f475991aea30a5f77eb6ef4335009595e69b7eb8c04bf970b4e7":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of d