r_northern_coin","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"veshzarzarzarven","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.macbeth.r1"}],"definition":"The silver coin demanded in the Scottish settlement with Norway. No conversion into another currency is specified.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.dollar_northern_coin.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"71d13f644ddc31ee0fffab0d26e6e0563418de26e15fe8d288f38fa149787de6":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.king-lear.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"dolfin","id":"shakespeare014.lex.dolphin_ballad_address","ipa":"","label":"dolphin_ballad_address","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"dolfin","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.king-lear.r1"}],"definition":"An address in Edgar's song. The local spelling allows a Dauphin echo without identifying any particular prince.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.dolphin_ballad_address.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"65fdf6e4a5482f452876c961c9160f220bfcf557235fe1d57416f9ebf7b85106":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic adaptation of a personal or place name.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic adaptation of a personal or place name.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"domitius","id":"shakespeare014.lex.domitius_enobarbus","ipa":"","label":"domitius_enobarbus","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"domitius","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"Domitius, the source\u2019s personal-name variant addressing Enobarbus. Same man as lex.enobarbus, not an extra entrant or a new officer.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.domitius_enobarbus.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"5e6480ab1a7dfb1d25a77bbd6dd2fd8a3a1cc30f6bd22e917c80fdbcdb305176":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-iv-part-2.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"domelton","id":"shakespeare014.lex.dommelton_merchant","ipa":"","label":"dommelton_merchant","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"domelton","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-iv-part-2.r1"}],"definition":"The merchant who refuses Falstaff and his companion Bardolph credit for satin.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.dommelton_merchant.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"93ec71cd69124540680fecde2cecdd8ddfac4805d3dc5183d9316210104f4566":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: lord","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.much-ado-about-nothing.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: lord","exampleIds":[],"headword":"arvenek","id":"shakespeare014.lex.don_aragon_honorific","ipa":"","label":"don_aragon_honorific","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"arvenek","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.much-ado-about-nothing.r1"}],"definition":"The Iberian honorific of Pedro and John, rendered as a native title.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.don_aragon_honorific.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"e852a9643b8baea2965f37413f03d1d232665923acc258df11b6fdd3f4855bd3":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare