ld, distinct from a merely small adult.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_infant.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"7c81331a946184346daf12a90e68731121377ba99899faa2e973cae41dae4679":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.richard-iii.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"lamf\u00ebrenm\u00e3n","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_interest_charge","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_interest_charge","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"lamf\u00fcrenmoin","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.richard-iii.r1"}],"definition":"An addition to the returned principal, here one kiss; not a percentage or a condemned rate imposed by the translator.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_interest_charge.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"e8133c1a06154c201a278f6f1c210e093340aca297f3313d6fa2cceed240abb3":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. A hard structural metal, named for the support a bone gives.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-vi-part-2.r2"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. A hard structural metal, named for the support a bone gives.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"kranzar","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_iron","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_iron","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"root","pronunciation":"kranzar","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-vi-part-2.r2"}],"definition":"iron metal","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_iron.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"9e6960b94411a2ae96c2e570186bc2c7dff7282cf3456cac4e0ed6956cb96f6f":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.king-john.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"kranzarvornvenor","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_iron_age_cruelty","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_iron_age_cruelty","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"kranzarvornvenor","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.king-john.r1"}],"definition":"The cruel Iron Age Arthur invokes as he pleads against the use of hot irons. The repetition of iron joins the mythic age to the metal.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_iron_age_cruelty.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"571bf883510281694f9d894529fd560e649164c401cf9568db111a511a4d8272":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-vi-part-2.r2"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"goryemsjo\u00d9","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_island","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_island","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"goryemsjong","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-vi-part-2.r2"}],"definition":"Land surrounded by water, the image of Lucrece\u2019s encircled body; not a newly named place.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_island.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"0edf8f89e6c48089fbe9d4ff5d2cc0315f276c9aee715cb954083aea2692f518":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.othello.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"y\u00eblyemardur\u00ebn","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_keel_ship","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_keel_ship","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"y\u00fclyemardur\u00fcn","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.othello.r1"}],"definition":"The long bottom structural part of a ship that cuts the water, used in the ploughing/wounding metaphor. No unstated dimensions or construction material.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_keel_ship.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"af92e9ff6e6834f9ccf1f7aba22faf2e56fa037305bcb7d1cc0d89387d43a209":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.much-ado-about-nothing.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"lilj\u00cden","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_key_music_pitch","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_key_music_pitch","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"lilj\u0117ren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.much-ado-about-nothing.r1"}],"definition":"The pitch or key in which to join the song, used figuratively to ask in what tone to answer Claudio.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_key_music_pitch.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"c21a167a6df8aa084a694d8107041f4524b217b3be558546ceac3359c0a2a4c1":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-vi-part-3.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"y\u00eblyemargl\u00c9z\u00cben","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_anchor_acts","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_anchor_acts","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"y\u00fclyemargl\u00e4zhwen","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-vi-part-3.r1"}],"definition":"Anchor,a vessel-holding device in Acts27,ship-hold. Distinguished from a ships internal hold or an abstract source of emotional stability;no unprinted material or design supplied.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_anchor_acts.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"e8cebd44e4d80a617d9196641c45dd663642951d4077135ae284251ab7dfcb41":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-viii.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"yemyatprodna","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_baptize","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_baptize","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"yemyatprodna","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-viii.r1"}],"definition":"Baptize:the source ritual washing,water-wash-set-apart. Retains baptism as its named act without specifying an unprinted mode of immersion or sprinkling;Spirit/fire uses remain the source's extensions of this same verb.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_baptize.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"25882dc1ff0fdf74f81069d48f36720f6aa9c66d8c5c7c7604ca771332d51cf0":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.loves-labors-lost.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"sh\u00ebralgiktenv\u00d7j\u00cden","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_bleat","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_bleat","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"sh\u00fcralgiktenv\u0113j\u0117ren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.loves-labors-lost.r1"}],"definition":"Make the characteristic cry of sheep or flock animals; sheep-voice, used nominally for bleatings.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_bleat.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"98004e84877d25b8b23690380ce8b4e760d82cafdcff337ac81f402431a509af":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-vi-part-2.r2"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"pelna boral","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_calf","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_calf","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"pelna boral","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-vi-part-2.r2"}],"definition":"A young bovine animal; source calf without an inferred sex.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_calf.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"655704e9dbadd538cfc42201cb8b5ee173f867775f9bd937d21bb3567a111ea3":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.pericles.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"y\u00eblyemarbra","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_caulk","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_caulk","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"y\u00fclyemarbra","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.pericles.r1"}],"definition":"Close or seal a vessel's seams against water,ship-close;the source calking trade without specifying a modern sealant or construction method. Agent derivation names a calker.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_caulk.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"49bd6946051f3a2b38e7d50686e8c329f1217077cc23c65692733e8bb8df8601":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.macbeth.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"se\u00dbthavvim","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_drowse","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_drowse","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"seshthavvim","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.macbeth.r1"}],"definition":"Drowsiness or sleep-heavy inactivity,sleep-near;Proverbs23:21personifies it as clothing a person in rags. This source's moral claim is not a clinical classification or a claim about every sleepy person.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_drowse.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"89e71b659999de8f52b631d34bedda2d18fed4479ad1995eecf35df6e4d02f66":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-vi-part-2.r2"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"h\u00c5b\u00cdthavvimswifl\u00dfn","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_familiar_spirit","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_familiar_spirit","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"h\u0101b\u0117rthavvimswifl\u014dn","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-vi-part-2.r2"}],"definition":"The spirit called familiar in the source divination category; not merely a familiar acquaintance or an ordinary friendly person.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_familiar_spirit.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"553abda033ef34221038641569104cf4bf7373946f7a125bbe6b3a71934aa392":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.richard-iii.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"nilomy\u00eblyemar","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_ferryboat","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_ferryboat","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"nilomy\u00fclyemar","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.richard-iii.r1"}],"definition":"A ferrying boat, river-ship, carrying the royal household across; keeps the supplied boat without importing an alternative ford reading or vessel design.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_ferryboat.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"5be68515c03ecd11c950522646e1bdc668f0cb5e03f1aba8246f5abb71e789c4":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-viii.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"felenyemyats\u00dflum","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_fuller","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_fuller","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"felenyemyats\u014dlum","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-viii.r1"}],"definition":"A worker who cleans or prepares cloth, cloth-wash-person; distinct from the adjective more full.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_fuller.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"7666a15904a2c36bde282302e97cc82b336387b6c45d9bd32a3fa7ef7361f515":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.macbeth.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"farp\u00e1f\u00d7j\u00cdtonda","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_gospel","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_gospel","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"farp\u00f4f\u0113j\u0117rtonda","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.macbeth.r1"}],"definition":"Gospel,the proclaimed good news of the kingdom in Matthew4:23;good-news. Not automatically a title of a completed written book.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_gospel.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"d2ebb96086f6ea7bb0f0ee3581638aea0c6d459621923f7feb55fb02174199f2":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-vi-part-2.r2"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"pelna zanna boral","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_heifer","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_heifer","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"pelna zanna boral","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-vi-part-2.r2"}],"definition":"A young female bovine in the source sacrificial list; not a generic animal nor an adult male ox.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_heifer.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"d2d3a1254df429dda806d9f41330e471dc39fa0d222d3408ef4e7ce6b4a19b17":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.othello.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"dar\u00c5elelyi\u00d1","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_hinge","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_hinge","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"dar\u0101elelyich","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.othello.r1"}],"definition":"A turning joint for a door, door-turn; no exact pivot or fastener design asserted.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_hinge.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"1ead2ff61d074df028e81dac8e9faffb3e94758f0fa1ba81d9482b615a319b8e":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-viii.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"pelnakr\u00c5v\u00ebm","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_kid","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_kid","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"pelnakr\u0101v\u00fcm","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-viii.r1"}],"definition":"A young goat, the source animal kid; not a human child.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_kid.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"bc1115e23efb584c81f712b37728c5d4ded1a5999053cbe1591ac884289c90f0":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.much-ado-about-nothing.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"bor\u00c5giktenv\u00d7j\u00cden","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_low_cattle","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_low_cattle","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"bor\u0101giktenv\u0113j\u0117ren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.much-ado-about-nothing.r1"}],"definition":"Make a bovine lowing sound, cow-voice; distinct from low position or rank.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_low_cattle.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"fa7be1ab641fca7538c6918547a9b70526feb05cf0090f9450f6681b46eb59d7":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-vi-part-3.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"y\u00eblyemarkoj","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_mast","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_mast","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"y\u00fclyemarkoj","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-vi-part-3.r1"}],"definition":"Mast,the ship's upright spar,ship-stand;Proverbs23:34places a precarious sleeper at its top. The verse supplies no rigging design,ship class or exact height.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_mast.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"a027b74fd19c406443f92e081f2a869208e6ca998011b80ac0480ce5d5afe178":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.much-ado-about-nothing.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"nelverj\u00c9gwa\u00c3l\u00dfn","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_perfume","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_perfume","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"nelverj\u00e4gwajzhl\u014dn","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.much-ado-about-nothing.r1"}],"definition":"A prepared fragrant mixture, here sacred incense; not necessarily an alcohol-based liquid fragrance.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_perfume.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"768cd776f87613ff4f4c835dd4ff01ab0eb89506a585f0584bd96b53f9cb46be":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.much-ado-about-nothing.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"nelverj\u00c9gwa\u00c3l\u00dfns\u00dflum","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_perfumer","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_perfumer","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"nelverj\u00e4gwajzhl\u014dns\u014dlum","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.much-ado-about-nothing.r1"}],"definition":"Maker or compounder of fragrant preparations, perfume-person; contextual source confectionary, not a sweets-maker. Easton dictionary entry at https://kingjamesbibledictionary.com/Dictionary/confection supports the historical contextual sense.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_perfumer.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"ce72fbf73d777961eff2d033905003f444c2c2eae746c6b2abaec738475c8dd6":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.julius-caesar.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"dar\u00c5el\u00e7l\u00d7on","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_porch","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_porch","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"dar\u0101el\u016bl\u0113on","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.julius-caesar.r1"}],"definition":"An entrance-side space or passage, door-place, in the supplied escape account. Does not prescribe a modern architectural plan.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_porch.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"9bae85df17aed756fde2ed592ce654c80d1707db20109e392d62b9ebe1554e14":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.julius-caesar.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"p\u00e1f\u00d7jw\u00ebnenplesten","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_refresh","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_refresh","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"p\u00f4f\u0113jw\u00fcnenplesten","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.julius-caesar.r1"}],"definition":"Restore vigour through relief or rest, here humans benefiting from cessation; not merely reload a display or replace an object.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_refresh.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"ed3cdd94b7ce273a2f57c31bad4e921d76e1ad1ceed1cd01c4b1bf4ed9b7010d":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-vi-part-2.r2"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"thani felenvorh\u00eb\u00d3","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_robe_train","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_robe_train","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"thani felenvorh\u00fcth","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-vi-part-2.r2"}],"definition":"Train of a robe,the trailing garment portion filling the temple in the vision; robe-tail,not teaching,a railway or a retinue.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_robe_train.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"760eb5c00e6d5460900e925d3d71991d0a0a42ab752a3aba07bc62cccf57b2c1":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.king-john.r1"}],"etymology":"Dramatic native reading. Preserve the native constituents in this dramatic sense.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"goryemsd\u00c7\u00d3s\u00dflum","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_sailor","ipa":"","label":"drama_native_kjv_sailor","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"goryemsd\u00e3ths\u014dlum","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.king-john.r1"}],"definition":"Sea-worker; a mariner, not the ship's master by default.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.drama_native_kjv_sailor.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"032ea8dca0e9f802905f9b68b49342bea3dca7f7dace1766e47d6a954