eare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"Erase a visible outline, dislimn in the changing-cloud comparison. Does not imply destroying a living horse.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.efface_shape.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"e2360d1d176901b681c4597aeae93627d88f12111c5e50a20dfefcaae4c34802":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_effeminate_label_corinthians","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_effeminate_label_corinthians","exampleIds":[],"headword":"salenamel","id":"shakespeare014.lex.effeminate_manner","ipa":"","label":"effeminate_manner","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"modifier","pronunciation":"salenamel","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"definition":"The feminine or soft behaviour in Ganymede\u2019s caricature of an inconstant youth, using native woman-soft. A reviewed dramatic manner-description rather than the earlier historical hostile-list category; no modern identity or specific sexual act is asserted.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.effeminate_manner.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"0f9c06a2fe7491b0e8581744a60b710a757e181b70c6335502167891c3107839":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of try","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of try","exampleIds":[],"headword":"kelde\u00dbon","id":"shakespeare014.lex.effort","ipa":"","label":"effort","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"keldeshon","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"definition":"Striving exertion, nominal use of try; the painter\u2019s strife to render lifelike blood.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.effort.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","