 or an assertion that he knows them.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.errand_task.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"90980ef3282d8caf110d9682bdf5f824a5ceead1512b8be02fb5580c3558d7fa":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: sea + sweet + root","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-merry-wives-of-windsor.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: sea + sweet + root","exampleIds":[],"headword":"goryemsmely\u00ebldur","id":"shakespeare014.lex.eryngo_candied_root","ipa":"","label":"eryngo_candied_root","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"goryemsmely\u00fcldur","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-merry-wives-of-windsor.r1"}],"definition":"Candied sea-holly root. Falstaff imagines a snow of these supposed aphrodisiacs.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.eryngo_candied_root.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"af2762c7643b9f70599ed7c55dc9eade4239fa198113c4ae604587122e6e716c":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.romeo-and-juliet.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"eskalus","id":"shakespeare014.lex.escalus_verona_prince","ipa":"","label":"escalus_verona_prince","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"eskalus","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.romeo-and-juliet.r1"}],"definition":"Prince of Verona, who judges the quarrel. Distinct from the Viennese lord.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.escalus_verona_prince.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"1f37df84e21937cc485ac7a2f4404ea3f852319cea975e2724916274b6d1fa8e":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespe