nt trips Goneril's steward.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.football_game.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"820caa9abc41466144d3addc502f298b024b8215769ee0f2fa4abd47e7f62cef":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Native lexical derivation from foot, mark","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"etymology":"Native lexical derivation from foot, mark","exampleIds":[],"headword":"palesden","id":"shakespeare014.lex.footprint","ipa":"","label":"footprint","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"palesden","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"definition":"A foot impression left on the ground, here absent from the sand.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.footprint.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"c3ca9498e54e67eab79c2612871ae05165db0989c41f796164eafbaff77d37fe":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native compound: foot + servant","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native compound: foot + servant","exampleIds":[],"headword":"palesd\u00c7v","id":"shakespeare014.lex.footservant_lackey","ipa":"","label":"footservant_lackey","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"palesd\u00e3v","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"definition":"An attending foot-servant, the impudent role Rosalind says she will play. Native foot + servant, not a character called Lackey or a borrowed class label.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.footservant_lackey.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"4d3e8fd99992493d1ca2d803178161df5ebf154a9c045f3a24598efb60f972ae":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Native lexical derivation from food, seek","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"etymology":"Native lexical derivation from food, seek","exampleIds":[],"headword":"d\u00cdn\u00d7rt\u00d7y\u00dfb\u00dfkelde\u00dbon","id":"shakespeare014.lex.forage","ipa":"","label":"forage","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"d\u0117rn\u0113rt\u0113y\u014db\u014dkeldeshon","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"definition":"Search/raid for sustenance, figuratively the pursuit of kisses as spoil.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.forage.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"4140328eba7b47f6072c096b90a94aab61b614639f73ba2e27b3b2db35e15652":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_ford","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_ford","exampleIds":[],"headword":"nilommarjo\u00d9","id":"shakespeare014.lex.ford","ipa":"","label":"ford","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"nilommarjong","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"definition":"A shallow watercourse crossing, opposed to deep channels in the grief/noise image.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.ford.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"334751af580321d6821862843888354215b8fe49264867c8244f2d01df91a110":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: ford","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-merry-wives-of-windsor.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: ford","exampleIds":[],"headword":"nilommarjo\u00d9","id":"shakespeare014.lex.ford_windsor_family","ipa":"","label":"ford_windsor_family","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"nilommarjong","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-merry-wives-of-windsor.r1"}],"definition":"The family name formed from a water crossing; helps maintain the stream-name jokes about Ford's assumed name.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.ford_windsor_family.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"66ef8fda1247e401c9b730e6ba7822d688f0eb5c4d7f0bed636c1a874c00877c":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"The Phoenix and Turtle: Native compound of before, come. One arriving ahead, an ominous precursor here. Native compositional agent stem; the modifier and fiend remain explicit.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-phoenix-and-turtle"}],"etymology":"The Phoenix and Turtle: Native compound of before, come. One arriving ahead, an ominous precursor here. Native compositional agent stem; the modifier and fiend remain explicit.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"p\u00e1nt\u00e7l","id":"shakespeare014.lex.forecomer","ipa":"","label":"forecomer","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"p\u00f4nt\u016bl","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-phoenix-and-turtle"}],"definition":"One arriving ahead, an ominous precursor here. Native compositional agent stem; the modifier and fiend remain explicit.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.forecomer.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"18ae908bd957c98e6046c51e92ad44968c2797187ed3f805ef5f3f0ee77ada82":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: staff + kjv_loop + leg","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.romeo-and-juliet.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: staff + kjv_loop + leg","exampleIds":[],"headword":"teralthirilviminolenpal","id":"shakespeare014.lex.foreign_r_letter","ipa":"","label":"foreign_r_letter","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"teralthirilviminolenpal","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.romeo-and-juliet.r1"}],"definition":"The foreign written R, described by its upright, upper loop and leg. The Nurse associates its sound with a dog's growl when she asks about the original names Romeo and rosemary.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.foreign_r_letter.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"01d296e6a902529e328c37988dea916aebd83548086020fc791b7c4415b552eb":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_foreknow_romans","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_foreknow_romans","exampleIds":[],"headword":"p\u00e1nh\u00c5b\u00cd","id":"shakespeare014.lex.foreknow","ipa":"","label":"foreknow","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb/noun","pronunciation":"p\u00f4nh\u0101b\u0117r","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"definition":"Know or perceive beforehand; the soul\u2019s foresight cannot prevent its faculties\u2019 rebellion. No theological predestination claim is imported.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.foreknow.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"f996ef52e4860a762226b39acd5ae747a5e271640133538c24c68d99a75a0402":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation: before + see","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation: before + see","exampleIds":[],"headword":"p\u00e1no\u00c3","id":"shakespeare014.lex.foresee_future","ipa":"","label":"foresee_future","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"p\u00f4nojzh","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"See what will come, contrasted by the soothsayer with making a fortune happen.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.foresee_future.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"42e2afe31612a9d2f980c4688d62c9b37eb3a48e0cb3b73e8d0f85f29dbc01ec":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native compound: forest + edge","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native compound: forest + edge","exampleIds":[],"headword":"y\u00ebljo\u00d9thren","id":"shakespeare014.lex.forest_purlieu","ipa":"","label":"forest_purlieu","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"y\u00fcljongthren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"definition":"Land at the outskirts or cleared margin of the forest, where Oliver seeks the sheepcote. Native forest-edge; not the whole forest interior or a claim about the precise legal boundary of a royal forest.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.forest_purlieu.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"2db107153a71aa38be6369b7ed9b57db575ff8207201579b60870ddf9c29f32a":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Native lexical derivation from before, sign","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"etymology":"Native lexical derivation from before, sign","exampleIds":[],"headword":"p\u00e1njelam","id":"shakespeare014.lex.forewarning","ipa":"","label":"forewarning","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"p\u00f4njelam","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"definition":"A sign of something to come, qualified as ill by the narrator; not independently asserted prophecy.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.forewarning.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"475efc4eda43873280ac549c678b5a72c3531f770f9fd8952b2e8a14ca5a8090":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native compound: branch + arrow + head","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native compound: branch + arrow + head","exampleIds":[],"headword":"y\u00eblenkerilharen","id":"shakespeare014.lex.forked_arrowhead","ipa":"","label":"forked_arrowhead","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"y\u00fclenkerilharen","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"definition":"The forked heads of hunting arrows, not the deer\u2019s antlers. Native branch + arrow + head retains the weapon shape without supplying an unprinted dimension.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.forked_arrowhead.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"e7d67911ce2cfc2a155cd3a26e5f0aae0137302726bcc0086816ae550220da87":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation: split + top","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation: split + top","exampleIds":[],"headword":"strasnaorthrenin","id":"shakespeare014.lex.forked_peak","ipa":"","label":"forked_peak","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"modifier","pronunciation":"strasnaorthrenin","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"A cleft or branching mountaintop in the changing cloud shapes; no utensil or invented measured height.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.forked_peak.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"c8f98168ce2d969536a84ba23af9280f44f378933b304d35ab696d07a5b27ad4":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Native lexical derivation from lose, hope","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"etymology":"Native lexical derivation from lose, hope","exampleIds":[],"headword":"b\u00e9rvven\u00e1l","id":"shakespeare014.lex.forlorn","ipa":"","label":"forlorn","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"modifier","pronunciation":"b\u00e9rvven\u00f4l","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"definition":"Abandoned in hope or deeply desolate, here the goddess\u2019s imagined state.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.forlorn.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"4149616ba4586708bdb0c46ecf031b738509a256a484069d64ffd7d84e480954":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Native lexical derivation from form, make","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"etymology":"Native lexical derivation from form, make","exampleIds":[],"headword":"l\u00dfna\u00d9","id":"shakespeare014.lex.form_make","ipa":"","label":"form_make","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"l\u014dnang","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"definition":"Shape or fashion something, including the heavenly moulds; not a style of clothing.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.form_make.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"10b9a560bd45486cffdda28a4320365f5a7cd14f028406bd62afb9c900e8b2fb":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation/sense: custom + form","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation/sense: custom + form","exampleIds":[],"headword":"venarl\u00dfn","id":"shakespeare014.lex.form_procedure","ipa":"","label":"form_procedure","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"venarl\u014dn","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"definition":"The customary procedure or manner required for receiving public honor, not merely the shape of an object or body.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.form_procedure.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"180d7133c9cdaec940aee2ac7805db830f82d010df46a47bb96dbacac6433d10":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of proper","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of proper","exampleIds":[],"headword":"tegliz","id":"shakespeare014.lex.formal_orderly","ipa":"","label":"formal_orderly","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"modifier","pronunciation":"tegliz","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"definition":"Regularly arranged according to convention, here the magistrate\u2019s beard cut. Does not denote a formal proof or official legal enactment.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.formal_orderly.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"598582b51632b297d60d12e634122ed8d5808fc007ef4d3cce89f19033efec52":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted geographic-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.macbeth.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted geographic-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"fores","id":"shakespeare014.lex.forres_scottish_town","ipa":"","label":"forres_scottish_town","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"fores","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.macbeth.r1"}],"definition":"The destination Banquo asks about when he sees the sisters.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.forres_scottish_town.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"93ed9c1589fc566d4e5bf0a5760c58f926a44b4dcc1cc8387f2efccc32e71ac4":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.richard-iii.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"forest","id":"shakespeare014.lex.forrest_princes_killer","ipa":"","label":"forrest_princes_killer","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"forest","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.richard-iii.r1"}],"definition":"One of Tyrrel's pair. His surname is distinct from a wood.","id":"shake