hing.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"hyu","id":"shakespeare014.lex.hugh_watchman_given","ipa":"","label":"hugh_watchman_given","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"hyu","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.much-ado-about-nothing.r1"}],"definition":"Hugh Oatcake, a watchman commended for his literacy.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.hugh_watchman_given.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"b4896eaa6290972fea71925669f5cf8601d0ae4a29fba225726bd91776eff121":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored short native lexical formation; motivation specified in definition, not a claimed attested historical change.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored short native lexical formation; motivation specified in definition, not a claimed attested historical change.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"sonum","id":"shakespeare014.lex.hum","ipa":"","label":"hum","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"sonum","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"definition":"Sustain a low voiced melody without articulated words; authored sound-family formation, used as accompaniment.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.hum.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"d386aa77e2bafed1b9b0a52b3bc84748117d9f9dfe6a9c8caba5c7b4da611361":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation/sense: hum","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation/sense: hum","exampleIds":[],"headword":"sonum","id":"shakespeare014.lex.hum_dismissive","ipa":"","label":"hum_dismissive","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"sonum","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"definition":"Make a low nonverbal dismissive sound at a petitioner, source Coriolanus humming at Cominius. Contextual extension of native hum; no song, tune or accompaniment is asserted.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.hum_dismissive.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"1e043b5daa59f7021da72b09ba3b94bb7476d4a5c80c0e289e6ead67e0f0246b":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation/sense: humanity","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation/sense: humanity","exampleIds":[],"headword":"s\u00dflum","id":"shakespeare014.lex.humane_treatment","ipa":"","label":"humane_treatment","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"modifier","pronunciation":"s\u014dlum","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"definition":"Showing humane concern rather than merely belonging to the human species.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.humane_treatment.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"17bfd82ce43ca60724b5536cd792c126a9a78750eb6fdfb6eab4417853bc1878":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of human","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of human","exampleIds":[],"headword":"s\u00dflum","id":"shakespeare014.lex.humanity","ipa":"","label":"humanity","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"s\u014dlum","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"definition":"Humane human nature invoked as a moral restraint; not a count of all living humans.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.humanity.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"8c2bc57c048046fd835544490f97a3241d0647918585390855c0b6535a7afed5":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of human","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of human","exampleIds":[],"headword":"s\u00dflum","id":"shakespeare014.lex.humanity_nature","ipa":"","label":"humanity_nature","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"s\u014dlum","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"The human nature or human frame steered by a spirit in Agrippa\u2019s praise. Nominal use of native human; distinct from benevolence alone or a count of all human beings.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.humanity_nature.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"da7b6bf0f8f9e743b7485fc06f15d32e96388c26fc3a37a7078ddb9b7eebb620":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: hair + bee","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.loves-labors-lost.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: hair + bee","exampleIds":[],"headword":"f\u00eblmelsav\u00ddlawin","id":"shakespeare014.lex.humblebee_verse","ipa":"","label":"humblebee_verse","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"f\u00fclmelsav\u012blawin","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.loves-labors-lost.r1"}],"definition":"The furry bee in Armado's three-animal verse.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.humblebee_verse.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"8b3883473c0e83bbafaf0bacb69d6ebdf0750215b5c8f174552727cd42e17741":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-vi-part-2.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"hyum","id":"shakespeare014.lex.hume_priest","ipa":"","label":"hume_priest","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronun