o\u2019s image for Adam\u2019s support. The native field-work compound does not imply marriage or a new plot of land.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.husbandry_cultivation.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"6906f4e8a1525a674ebe2f6dbd03aab24804ed66ce2f80d6fb2f368442de60f7":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation/sense: house + manage","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation/sense: house + manage","exampleIds":[],"headword":"z\u00e1lk\u00c7fag\u00eba","id":"shakespeare014.lex.husbandry_management","ipa":"","label":"husbandry_management","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"z\u00f4lk\u00e3fag\u00fca","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"definition":"Prudent management or stewardship, here of the Volscian polity. Native house-manage used nominally; not marital conduct or literal farming.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.husbandry_management.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"fbab939ef8cdd1cd859aebd5f9b1cc5ddf5020e77cda1a0d4d4ff06dd8a35d33":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_husk","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_husk","exampleIds":[],"headword":"nelshalem","id":"shakespeare014.lex.husks_food","ipa":"","label":"husks_food","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"nelshalem","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"definition":"Outer plant coverings eaten with the hogs in Orlando\u2019s prodigal-son allusion. No particular species is asserted.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.husks_food.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"b175b7d16184d2a2f4d85cdf804a602f0d4ac67e42767edeb5b72170ec49563f":{"audioLinks":[],