isgrace or a discredited reputation, distinguished from the private emotion of remorse.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.infamy.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"8d268d004dd8f2aec3cda1204e5f1f669b4ead341454e76e5586c7dd4caa6abf":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_infant","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_infant","exampleIds":[],"headword":"nevpel","id":"shakespeare014.lex.infant","ipa":"","label":"infant","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"nevpel","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"definition":"A very young child, distinct from a merely small adult.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.infant.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"a59a7bbe1141cd8633bb1fcd68de9f054015395572a2a19ca2adb10dea685318":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: infant + cloth","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-winters-tale.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: infant + cloth","exampleIds":[],"headword":"nevpelfelen","id":"shakespeare014.lex.infant_bearing_cloth","ipa":"","label":"infant_bearing_cloth","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"nevpelfelen","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-winters-tale.r1"}],"definition":"The fine carrying or ceremonial cloth that suggests the exposed infant belongs to a family of rank.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.infant_bearing_cloth.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"c42a3509e43c49fa44e85d984b38ddf5065efefeae736886622b9beb2277e83f":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of dote","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of dote","exampleIds":[],"headword":"sil\u00ebm","id":"shakespeare014.lex.infatuation","ipa":"","label":"infatuation","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"sil\u00fcm","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"definition":"Foolish consuming attachment or fixation; nominal use of dote, not innocent imaginative fancy.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.infatuation.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"b0c6058cf1c8f1a9679d541bed698417d0b42b1fdebf06858d08c2ff9ccd85c9":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation: illness + give","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation: illness + give","exampleIds":[],"headword":"murenf\u00c5w","id":"shakespeare014.lex.infect_contagion","ipa":"","label":"infect_contagion","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"murenf\u0101w","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"Transmit harmful illness, metaphorically the bad news affecting its teller; no literal disease is diagnosed.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.infect_contagion.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"290fe0c8842c276341d7019f7160950a2ea35e760919fdab71bc594cbe5a2bfb":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Native lexical derivation from sick, spread","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"etymology":"Native lexical derivation from sick, spread","exampleIds":[],"headword":"murvorstrasf\u00c5w","id":"shakespeare014.lex.infection","ipa":"","label":"infection","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"murvorstrasf\u0101w","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"definition":"Spreading sickness in the plague-year conceit, without adding an unstated organism or medical theory.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.infection.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"2eb7bb8d5a8f85930a18d415862cb525fef3bc16b8e575bb0135a332f0c4da8c":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation: sickness + give","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation: sickness + give","exampleIds":[],"headword":"murenf\u00c5w","id":"shakespeare014.lex.infectious_quality","ipa":"","label":"infectious_quality","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"modifier","pronunciation":"murenf\u0101w","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"Able to transmit illness, the pestilence Cleopatra wishes on the messenger. Native sickness-give; records the curse without an editorial claim that illness was transmitted.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.infectious_quality.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"2be21f0b25e9a65eaa660037b05aa95ed5f1499e4c17cd7b46b0881c58725289":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native lexical derivation: fire + cause","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native lexical derivation: fire + cause","exampleIds":[],"headword":"zarunh\u00eb","id":"shakespeare014.lex.inflame","ipa":"","label":"inflame","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"zarunh\u00fc","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"definition":"Set alight or excite desire, preserving the passion/fire metaphor.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.inflame.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"53f8c9e9997f276a37c165d84013e753135839c3624e3e3c6acc698946632f4c":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation/sense: know + cause","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation/sense: know + cause","exampleIds":[],"headword":"h\u00c5b\u00cdh\u00eb","id":"shakespeare014.lex.inform_news","ipa":"","label":"inform_news","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"h\u0101b\u0117rh\u00fc","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"definition":"Make someone aware of news, the Senate being possessed of the return and success; not demonic possession or property ownership.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.inform_news.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"3c6e7998d25d6f66ce710c92710af0e3210f293babfb17a6efc3804d5585324a":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation/sense: favour + seek","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation/sense: favour + seek","exampleIds":[],"headword":"m\u00ddnam\u00d7t\u00d7y\u00dfb\u00dfkelde\u00dbon","id":"shakespeare014.lex.ingratiate_gesture","ipa":"","label":"ingratiate_gesture","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"modifier","pronunciation":"m\u012bnam\u0113t\u0113y\u014db\u014dkeldeshon","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"definition":"Seeking favor through a gesture, source insinuating nod. The practiced deference is explicitly counterfeit in Coriolanus\u2019s own speech.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.ingratiate_gesture.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"8233a97090c4fd1203dba3135b87910d867abdea72e689cbec50f0eafe03b097":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of ungrateful","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of ungrateful","exampleIds":[],"headword":"mafarbroft","id":"shakespeare014.lex.ingratitude_failure","ipa":"","label":"ingratitude_