e in the medicinal analogy.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.ingredient.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"512db380a8c0eb9f6e7135b80588a4362b38f274fafc1e351077eaa5fe12d412":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_iniquity","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_iniquity","exampleIds":[],"headword":"murlametfalnthren","id":"shakespeare014.lex.iniquity","ipa":"","label":"iniquity","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"murlametfalnthren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"definition":"Wrongdoing that royal authority ought to oppose; moral action rather than the feeling of guilt.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.iniquity.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"61f9d013eb58c73625c157542653b090705c5eb2947e3476d2670a7cce402653":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: iniquity","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.richard-iii.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: iniquity","exampleIds":[],"headword":"murlametfalnthren","id":"shakespeare014.lex.iniquity_morality_vice","ipa":"","label":"iniquity_morality_vice","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"murlametfalnthren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.richard-iii.r1"}],"definition":"The stage Vice Iniquity in Richard's aside about speaking with two meanings. A native name for personified wrongdoing.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.iniquity_morality_vice.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"97c45e29deebc9601e739c5224d289a96ec67278239802509a59bcc453b12709":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of iniquity","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense o