ors-lost.r1"}],"definition":"The woman Costard is accused of meeting in the park.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.jaquenetta_countrywoman.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"3c94dab3825edecb2d734d10fd8e4437c409f3f13320664dfb3b8b7691a12620":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic adaptation of a personal name.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic adaptation of a personal name.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"\u00c3ak","id":"shakespeare014.lex.jaques_brother","ipa":"","label":"jaques_brother","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"jzhak","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"definition":"The brother whom Oliver keeps at school. Distinct from the melancholy courtier Jaques and the pilgrimage Saint Jaques in another play.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.jaques_brother.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"24b4870983d49ae7ec66a6f62b0863224a22e0b3149bd964388d4f71c4ee766a":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic adaptation of a personal name.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic adaptation of a personal name.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"\u00c3ak","id":"shakespeare014.lex.jaques_courtier","ipa":"","label":"jaques_courtier","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"jzhak","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"definition":"The melancholy courtier with Duke Senior, distinct from Orlando\u2019s school-going brother Jaques and the pilgrimage Saint Jaques. No identity qualifier prints in the name.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.jaques_courtier.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"8a37aa268774605950156ad53efd42753f4c459333e12