"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"jov","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"The Roman divine name Jove in Menas\u2019s earthly-sovereignty comparison. Same figure as Jupiter; explicit case-correct name display, not an ordinary borrowed word for a god.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.jove_roman.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"d4793cd6e1713037fc0c5b4db7a144ecd253fed48b99c15bc0496405887ab7ab":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.titus-andronicus.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"jubiter","id":"shakespeare014.lex.jubiter_countryman_misnaming","ipa":"","label":"jubiter_countryman_misnaming","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"jubiter","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.titus-andronicus.r1"}],"definition":"The country fellow\u2019s mispronunciation of Jupiter, whom he takes for someone he might have met. Preserve the distinction from the deity\u2019s name.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.jubiter_countryman_misnaming.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"035e589b676dde5d7a9d307e80443684c3149fe2b4ede2612f3c71231d8d105e":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_judas_iscariot","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_judas_iscariot","exampleIds":[],"headword":"judas","id":"shakespeare014.lex.judas_betrayer","ipa":"","label":"judas_betrayer","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"judas","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"definition":"Judas the betrayer in Celia\u2019s hair and kiss joke, with the source short name only. Distinct from other Judas/Judah identities; no reference label or Iscariot is added to the printed name.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.judas_betrayer.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"28c25881c5ae7443026750e76f6688c48d61f12bef7b902217b30d8638925c8a":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.loves-labors-lost.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"judas","id":"shakespeare014.lex.judas_maccabaeus_given","ipa":"","label":"judas_maccabaeus_given","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"judas","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.loves-labors-lost.r1"}],"definition":"The given name of the Worthy Judas Maccabaeus, whom the other players confuse with Iscariot.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.judas_maccabaeus_given.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"09e31fabdc090163a2998c048f54596e1e830ed7272481435584d1e9d53ebe07":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.loves-labors-lost.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"judas makabeus","id":"shakespeare014.lex.judas_maccabaeus_role","ipa":"","label":"judas_maccabaeus_role","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"judas makabeus","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.loves-labors-lost.r1"}],"definition":"The Worthy Judas Maccabaeus in the pageant. Distinct from Judas Iscariot and from the schoolmaster playing this role.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.judas_maccabaeus_role.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"7e6e6ea028c40b1f5fc47a4f2db71466f5db964de1cac3e5b2eafb4705906a43":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.loves-labors-lost.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"jud","id":"shakespeare014.lex.jude_stage_fragment","ipa":"","label":"jude_stage_fragment","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"jud","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.loves-labors-lost.r1"}],"definition":"A clipped form of the stage Judas's given name in the courtiers' donkey-name joke.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.jude_stage_fragment.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"06b8b1aeb115c6fbac069477b1f821dd2f6d05d3f23cf68a5520367fe4ecf7c8":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of kjv_judea","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of kjv_judea","exampleIds":[],"headword":"judea","id":"shakespeare014.lex.judea_region","ipa":"","label":"judea_region","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"judea","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"The geographical Jewry to which Alexas went on Antony\u2019s affairs, not a generic designation of Jewish people or a borrowed ordinary noun.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.judea_region.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"a5f26eff640c4bab6decb58098030e3bb7e8938507b438595a744adb5074853f":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation/sense: money + punishment_penalty","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation/sense: money + punishment_penalty","exampleIds":[],"headword":"zar