dio in the prince's company.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.love_claudio_mock_title.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"335b93802a027c492ac2cc8f13247dc24b33d6e92837e1f147f0f79584d7038a":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native lexical derivation: time + grant","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.shakespeares-sonnets.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native lexical derivation: time + grant","exampleIds":[],"headword":"venor\u00c3ahf\u00c5w","id":"shakespeare014.lex.love_lease","ipa":"","label":"love_lease","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"venorjzhahf\u0101w","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.shakespeares-sonnets.r1"}],"definition":"A grant of tenure for a term, metaphorically the duration allotted to true love in Sonnet 107. Native time-grant, distinct from a permanent gift or a particular monetary rent.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.love_lease.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"8398e08117c94132062dbd4bfd9108bd04321f1f7ff0b788fbc2de381ac1d48d":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of love","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of love","exampleIds":[],"headword":"a\u00d9z","id":"shakespeare014.lex.love_mock_title","ipa":"","label":"love_mock_title","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"angz","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"definition":"The personified mock address Signior Love, directed to Orlando. Native love receives proper-name Maxima in this epithet; no new person or foreign ordinary word is introduced.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.love_mock_title.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"b772f88b2a6e40836ee82dc080019655799a4687c1d6a2125e93a90249a988f0":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of love","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of love","exampleIds":[],"headword":"a\u00d9z","id":"shakespeare014.lex.love_personified","ipa":"","label":"love_personified","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"angz","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"definition":"Love invoked by Tarquin as a divinity and guide; retains the native love word, not a new foreign deity label.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.love_personified.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"2425c7d86f637104ddbbf5bdf210d6b84fc3f1427ae2f9482f61c370c233adb5":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of love","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of love","exampleIds":[],"headword":"a\u00d9z","id":"shakespeare014.lex.love_personified_feminine","ipa":"","label":"love_personified_feminine","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"angz","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"Personified Love invoked with her soft hours in Antony\u2019s speech. Native love form with Maxima; no forced replacement by the masculine Cupid or an unprinted proper name Venus.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.love_personified_feminine.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"50b86cb208845732f49fd90d1a44a4a17ca6bd4506e7690d0e477de345938ee8":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.richard-iii.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"lovel","id":"shakespeare014.lex.lovell_richards_agent","ipa":"","label":"lovell_richard