e-for-measure.r1"}],"definition":"The constable's wife whose visit to the house is disputed. Her title accompanies the family's anatomical name.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.mistress_elbow_wife.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"c9f61c988ae49e719063ba0cc3ba37a05acaa28ea77e57a48f02e8a61e7a8f86":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of doubt","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of doubt","exampleIds":[],"headword":"lamves","id":"shakespeare014.lex.mistrust","ipa":"","label":"mistrust","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"lamves","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"definition":"Suspicion directed at another\u2019s motives or knowledge, beyond simple uncertainty.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.mistrust.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"d98b5244a355a6f717738a4dfd30fbfc2d32e60c2a4844f4266bb6fdeafa2dcb":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic adaptation of a personal or place name.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic adaptation of a personal or place name.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"mitridates","id":"shakespeare014.lex.mithridates_comagen","ipa":"","label":"mithridates_comagen","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"mitridates","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"Mithridates, explicitly the king of Comagen in this roster. Not silently merged with a different Pontic king of the same name.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.mithridates_comagen.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"e77e32f41cc1cdc551067bbeabd11f271aaec7e63144b7c5bab850d6156a2890":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: relief_ease","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.measure-for-measure.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: relief_ease","exampleIds":[],"headword":"venel","id":"shakespeare014.lex.mitigation_bawds_nickname","ipa":"","label":"mitigation_bawds_nickname","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"venel","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.measure-for-measure.r1"}],"definition":"Lucio's ironic alternative address to Mistress Overdone, a name of easing her clients' troubles.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.mitigation_bawds_nickname.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"80461abf781855d5d77ec82db07507af9ab3ec0614a2a9ef45bd2180d8ac066e":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native lexical derivation: sorrow + sound","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native lexical derivation: sorrow + sound","exampleIds":[],"headword":"w\u00e9asemson","id":"shakespeare014.lex.moan_native","ipa":"","label":"moan_native","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun/verb","pronunciation":"w\u00e9asemson","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"definition":"A low sustained expression of grief, native sorrow-sound; distinct from the physical groan and replacing undocumented mon\u00ebl.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.moan_native.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"0cb4976a5c58ff0415a2a38a5ed29d1f5e113500dcd3b360ec47c00474536430":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: wrap + head","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.hamlet.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: wrap + head","exampleIds":[],"headword":"feleno\u00c3t\u00e7haren","id":"shakespeare014.lex.mobled_queen_epithet","ipa":"","label":"mobled_queen_epithet","notes":"","ortho