oth in Valeria\u2019s Penelope joke; native cloth-insect names this source category, not every insect found on cloth.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.moth_cloth.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"dd01b7ad8819b6de5adf4b299f90cb272ef8270e26a589e781301b7a9e0fe500":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: rise + grief","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.king-lear.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: rise + grief","exampleIds":[],"headword":"ner\u00c3\u00cdw\u00e9asem","id":"shakespeare014.lex.mother_rising_fit","ipa":"","label":"mother_rising_fit","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"nerjzh\u0117rw\u00e9asem","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.king-lear.r1"}],"definition":"Lear calls the mounting distress in his body the mother. It rises toward his heart and he commands it down.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.mother_rising_fit.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"3f7edf3166bfab65551ac10900871f9463ba51f226946d7f51ad4e93306856bd":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation/sense: cause","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation/sense: cause","exampleIds":[],"headword":"h\u00eb","id":"shakespeare014.lex.motion_stimulus","ipa":"","label":"motion_stimulus","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"h\u00fc","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"definition":"A slight prompting occasion or provocation for anger, source motion; not only bodily movement or a formal parliamentary proposal.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.motion_stimulus.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"585e626e580bf604d2bb7858661f8bb842a96891a4cc33ffa1981286aad00359":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored