 of the native object form of I in Henry V 4.4.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-v.r1"}],"etymology":"Source-specific reanalysis of the native object form of I in Henry V 4.4.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"r\u00e1get","id":"shakespeare014.lex.moy_pistol_coin","ipa":"","label":"moy_pistol_coin","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"r\u00f4get","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-v.r1"}],"definition":"Pistol hears French moi as a unit of ransom. The native pseudo-coin repeats the sound of the first-person object pronoun.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.moy_pistol_coin.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"e6a310ab8d75d6c9a612f032d2d268c499f6093bc35b0ec20d25f8072a5b6d49":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-two-gentlemen-of-verona.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"moyses","id":"shakespeare014.lex.moyses_forest_outlaw","ipa":"","label":"moyses_forest_outlaw","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"moyses","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-two-gentlemen-of-verona.r1"}],"definition":"Member of the forest band pursuing Eglamour. This is a separate person from the biblical Moses.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.moyses_forest_outlaw.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"e886f56402d492d6233711ed7891a820ae8078b78307a8b6a458850ebafd55da":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Selected from the existing native performance refrain to preserve the two nonnys of Balthasar's song.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.much-ado-about-nothing.r1"}],"etymology":"Selected from the existing native performance refrain to preserve the two nonnys of Balthasar's song.","exampleIds":[]