 card mark above the game total in Grumio's two-and-thirty joke.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.pip_card_mark.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"1968bf19d180812b124c74db539ce0981353a204207a05a0c93b6a9e8aeac096":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: finger + hole","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.hamlet.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: finger + hole","exampleIds":[],"headword":"jeldul","id":"shakespeare014.lex.pipe_finger_stop","ipa":"","label":"pipe_finger_stop","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"jeldul","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.hamlet.r1"}],"definition":"A pipe opening a player closes or opens with the finger to choose a note; Fortune imagines playing a person in this way.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.pipe_finger_stop.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"e3e2107ed0afc3e2981e4532cdcba625f2e9faa6093972c0986685fccee797f7":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: seed + apple","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-merry-wives-of-windsor.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: seed + apple","exampleIds":[],"headword":"p\u00e1inv\u00dfrmel","id":"shakespeare014.lex.pippin_dessert_apple","ipa":"","label":"pippin_dessert_apple","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"p\u00f4inv\u014drmel","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-merry-wives-of-windsor.r1"}],"definition":"An eating apple served with cheese at the end of dinner. Distinct from King Pippin.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.pippin_dessert_apple.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"8d41af5efe0ec6d3756666cbef26bc1cfc932f0aee911cf3dcc8bfa6c431a5f4":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name ada