"","label":"plaintiff_court_claimant","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"lamettondas\u014dlum","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.much-ado-about-nothing.r1"}],"definition":"The party bringing a claim. Dogberry twice applies the title to prisoners who are accused.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.plaintiff_court_claimant.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"a091cc1f89c9a84d482aea32db9c9af8cd8797dac8e76b2230a4a05f5c707c1c":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: broad + canopy + tree","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-two-noble-kinsmen.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: broad + canopy + tree","exampleIds":[],"headword":"gimkinkov\u00ebry\u00eblverzet","id":"shakespeare014.lex.plane_spreading_tree","ipa":"","label":"plane_spreading_tree","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"gimkinkov\u00fcry\u00fclverzet","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-two-noble-kinsmen.r1"}],"definition":"The broad-spreading plane tree against which the quoted cedar's spreading crown is compared.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.plane_spreading_tree.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"bf7defef688685413d865763f09d6f62a9776b165bac0e4619fbae7cffb35fdd":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation: wander + star","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation: wander + star","exampleIds":[],"headword":"m\u00e5rmaserb\u00e7orin","id":"shakespeare014.lex.planet_wandering_star","ipa":"","label":"planet_wandering_star","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"mourmaserb\u016borin","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"A wandering celestial body in the source\u2019s astrological classification, which includes the moon. Native wandering-star, not a modern scientific recategorization.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.planet_wandering_star.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"233db1d767c696055a1a136ab1de8566d41be4ec75d98978dc3051bba653691b":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation: wood + flat","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation: wood + flat","exampleIds":[],"headword":"y\u00eblshalin","id":"shakespeare014.lex.plank_board","ipa":"","label":"plank_board","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"y\u00fclshalin","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"A flat length of timber used in a ship, the veteran\u2019s rotten-planks warning. Native wood-flat; the adjective rotten remains his accusation rather than an inspection finding.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.plank_board.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"57df14fd08799b812f5ee1fc7d7ace6dfec37006965dabe55e6fc33591754382":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_plant_stock","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_plant_stock","exampleIds":[],"headword":"verzetvor","id":"shakespeare014.lex.plant_stock","ipa":"","label":"plant_stock","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"verzetvor","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"definition":"Rooted plant stock in the graft/fruit lineage image; not commercial stock, cattle or financial interest.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.plant_stock.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"9d1946485e6d649d9fc7