he preceding cosmic-pocket simile. Native metal-vessel does not invent an exact material, itemized vessel shapes, or amount.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.plate_valuable_ware.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"d21e90cbb0bab422228af56528ddfd9d7ac54b8bd1d8a80bcdc0189453075bbc":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.hamlet.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"plautus","id":"shakespeare014.lex.plautus_writer","ipa":"","label":"plautus_writer","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"plautus","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.hamlet.r1"}],"definition":"The author whom Polonius invokes for comic lightness.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.plautus_writer.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"4e567f67b7e3367a71dc56f48b966f8072b94e9267a0be139313dce2ece09289":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of play","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.shakespeares-sonnets.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of play","exampleIds":[],"headword":"faln","id":"shakespeare014.lex.play_music","ipa":"","label":"play_music","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"faln","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.shakespeares-sonnets.r1"}],"definition":"Perform on a musical instrument in Sonnet 128; a musical extension of the native play root rather than a game or theatrical role.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.play_music.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"7a38709a73ce7117002961f024e170ad802d1fc43bc941a60ac2af2d5358162d":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation: play + leaf","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation: play + leaf","exampleIds":[],"headword":"falny\u00eblet","id":"shakespeare014.lex.playing_card","ipa":"","label":"playing_card","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"falny\u00fclet","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"A marked playing leaf in the metaphor of secretly arranged cards; not a greeting card or a written letter.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.playing_card.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"46dd8ee3bb9b969d3de9b34da63ec3f1efa0c3b64daf66eb17fb1bf47d078fda":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of plead","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of plead","exampleIds":[],"headword":"w\u00cf\u00dfhoren","id":"shakespeare014.lex.plea","ipa":"","label":"plea","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"w\u00cf\u014dhoren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"definition":"An appeal or argument offered in a case; no lawful hearing is available in the metaphorical court.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.plea.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"3ebc8f724f624d292c32e34beeeb5834db85678986c006c097ccd18c7882b9ff":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of delight","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of delight","exampleIds":[],"headword":"pisensem","id":"shakespeare014.lex.please_delight","ipa":"","label":"please_delight","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"pisensem","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"Give pleasure or satisfaction to a person, the envoy\u2019s claim about Caesar\u2019s response. Explicit transitive verbal use of native delight, distinct from a courteous please request particle.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.please_delight.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"4ad14efd9658457a58c3ff691722f0ba05b7f1141558dc55d646bb6cdc43a178":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of delight","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.shakespeares-sonnets.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of delight","exampleIds":[],"headword":"pisensem","id":"shakespeare014.lex.pleasure_delight","ipa":"","label":"pleasure_delight","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"pisensem","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.shakespeares-sonnets.r1"}],"definition":"Give pleasure, or be pleased in passive voice; the ears denying pleasure in the beloved\u2019s tune in Sonnet 141.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.pleasure_delight.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"e8c54e301d595a11754b004b6543ce2e9d0808f2e72d2cfd84994758ea68a6b7":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native lexical derivation: cloth + bend","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native lexical derivation: cloth + bend","exampleIds":[],"headword":"felenlunor","id":"shakespeare014.lex.pleat","ipa":"","label":"pleat","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"felenlunor","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"definition":"A fold in fabric, the pleats of majesty hiding baseness; distinct from a crease in skin.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.pleat.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"07cc8eeba189cddd977ceec7bfd0a8ab4470dded1c7973337ca9195dbebbf408":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sen