 land used for the improvement that frank rebuke brings. Distinct from hearing with an ear.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.ploughing_tillage.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"a3fddcc97adddfd195f416298d2c48d64666ca0f54cad9c40a1d6f967ff3405e":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored short native lexical root; no claim of historical attestation.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored short native lexical root; no claim of historical attestation.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"vemul","id":"shakespeare014.lex.plum","ipa":"","label":"plum","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"vemul","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"definition":"The fruit named plum in the ripe/unripe comparison, a native fruit-family root inspired by venam; no cultivar is invented.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.plum.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"817a243dba3f0219409d4dd128afb8eaff785da4f9acf233acb5c9cc2659775a":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Native lexical derivation from flesh, full","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"etymology":"Native lexical derivation from flesh, full","exampleIds":[],"headword":"vorinplesten","id":"shakespeare014.lex.plump","ipa":"","label":"plump","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"modifier","pronunciation":"vorinplesten","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"definition":"Rounded and full in bodily flesh, not a stomach full after eating.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.plump.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"7ade4c4784dd69aafee9894ed960b81ba30ef13660a4634463ad678d35ece8f1":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Permitted sound adaptation of a source personal or place name; no claim of a historical sound law.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"etymology":"Permitted sound adaptation of a source personal or place name; no claim of a historical sound law.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"pluton","id":"shakespeare014.lex.pluto","ipa":"","label":"pluto","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"pluton","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"definition":"The mythic underworld ruler in the Orpheus comparison, not the modern astronomical body.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.pluto.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"f31eb83a6399c0878187e97ed4c7ea00f2046e180e28e1f3e495e5c0b8ef9f25":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted geographic-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.king-john.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted geographic-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"po","id":"shakespeare014.lex.po_italian_river","ipa":"","label":"po_italian_river","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"po","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.king-john.r1"}],"definition":"The river in Philip's mock display of travel conversation.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.po_italian_river.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"e6c0c1ccd4ae268e9f80646cd8cd19934e03e20faafbb014a0cfe176293b6163":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native compound: seed + cover","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native compound: seed + cover","exampleIds":[],"headword":"p\u00e1inshalen","id":"shakespeare014.lex.pod_shell","ipa":"","label":"pod_shell","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"p\u00f4inshalen","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"definition":"A seed-bearing plant pod or its enclosing shell, source cods. Native seed + cover; the source count is two pods, not two individual peas.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.pod_shell.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"21508c63cee785a5a819aa4eca1b59d2a73ce9d52f07fd1b2dd53e34077c98c0":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Native lexical derivation from smooth","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"etymology":"Native lexical derivation from smooth","exampleIds":[],"headword":"ma\u2019siv\u00ebl","id":"shakespeare014.lex.poem_unpolished","ipa":"","label":"poem_unpolished","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"modifier","pronunciation":"ma\u2019siv\u00fcl","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"definition":"Unpolished in craft: source\u2019s modesty formula for the author\u2019s verses, not a factual claim about their worth.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.poem_unpolished.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"4fa6cd7b9e56a9941d2951f1f233d30dc6e194e8824439a40f58e6d0d1169f5d":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of thought","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.shakespeares-sonnets.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of thought","exampleIds":[],"headword":"w\u00c5vumen","id":"shakespeare014.lex.poetic_conceit","ipa":"","label":"poetic_conceit","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"w\u0101vumen","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.shakespeares-sonnets.r1"}],"definition":"A mental conception of transient life in Sonnet 15; no conceited vanity is implied.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.poetic_conceit.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"ab1b8ad2d0ab085fe522e2606f1d063c6f9f9da42979061ae3ce658009623431":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of fre