,"id":"shakespeare014.lex.pole_suffolk","ipa":"","label":"pole_suffolk","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"pol","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.henry-vi-part-1.r1"}],"definition":"Family name of William de la Pole, Earl of Suffolk.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.pole_suffolk.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"14f502102d4e898490d7444e4c46ea91a8f92d57d3643ab7d60466f1027d0515":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic adaptation of a personal or place name.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic adaptation of a personal or place name.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"polemon","id":"shakespeare014.lex.polemon_king","ipa":"","label":"polemon_king","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"polemon","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"Polemon in the paired kings of Mede and Lycaonia roster. Preserve the local grouping rather than correcting the drama by external historical geography.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.polemon_king.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"1bbdeb60703a9b5bbc1e30e66fed54581b90052b1dbd8be4f6f458cc806f4914":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Native lexical derivation from smooth, shine","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"etymology":"Native lexical derivation from smooth, shine","exampleIds":[],"headword":"siv\u00eblb\u00e7oren","id":"shakespeare014.lex.polish","ipa":"","label":"polish","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"siv\u00fclb\u016boren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"definition":"Rub a surface to a smooth shine; figuratively the sun makes hill and tree tops look like polished gold.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.polish.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"3d1afe0d8cf600c0a3fb66d2fca7482460c83cc49c7fb82d1c694cddd033d643":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: manner + shape","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.cymbeline.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: manner + shape","exampleIds":[],"headword":"f\u00c7ll\u00dfn","id":"shakespeare014.lex.polish_manners","ipa":"","label":"polish_manners","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"f\u00e3ll\u014dn","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.cymbeline.r1"}],"definition":"Shape or cultivate someone\u2019s manners by example. The mature courtiers see their model in Posthumus as in a mirror. This is an interpretation of feated.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.polish_manners.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"7c0389e9659e6eb86b405e3f9c196921a60b06e0ee4262abd8cf52edc1e66a64":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation: divide + group","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation: divide + group","exampleIds":[],"headword":"threnina\u00d9gur","id":"shakespeare014.lex.political_faction","ipa":"","label":"political_faction","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"threninanggur","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"A politically divided party or interest group, born of rival domestic powers; no invented modern party name.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.political_faction.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"797dda12301d9988bcf14cb9affa69017abd4fb60e19078b9b04be624d244a96":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation/sense: change + person","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation/sense: change + person","exampleIds":[],"headword":"\u00e3lums\u00dflum","id":"shakespeare014.lex.political_innovator","ipa":"","label":"political_innovator","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"oilums\u014dlum","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"definition":"A person attempting political change in Sicinius\u2019s treason charge. Native change-person; not a modern technological entrepreneur and not a narrator verdict of guilt.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.political_innovator.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"229bf686eb617053b5e42918c2532e546022deaeae356326bf4badf4944f8553":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of command","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of command","exampleIds":[],"headword":"nor\u00d3a","id":"shakespeare014.lex.political_mandate","ipa":"","label":"political_mandate","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"northa","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"An authoritative political command, quoted mockingly as Caesar\u2019s in 1.1. Not a modern electoral mandate or an invented quantity.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.political_mandate.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"2840dcfb09ab700d36fc224df19a0ea037535985bbde4b659c3b2e6e9eb8932b":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native lexical derivation: people + rule","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native lexical derivation: people + rule","exampleIds":[],"headword":"s\u00dflumvar\u00dfnen","id":"shakespeare014.lex.political_rule","ipa":"","label":"political_rule","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"s\u014dlumvar\u014dnen","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"definition":"The exercise and organization of public rule, which changes from kings to consuls.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.political_rule.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"13d892d9eb0db9c9d4ed08b3410230cedfd5320842b1889465b4a82cf350e126":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation/sense: community + rule","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation/sense: community + rule","exampleIds":[],"headword":"\u00e1pe\u00dbemvar\u00dfnen","id":"shakespeare014.lex.political_state","ipa":"","label":"political_state","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"\u00f4peshemvar\u014dnen","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"definition":"The civic body and its government, source state or weal. Distinct from an enduring condition and from one person\u2019s landed estate; no modern national boundaries are asserted.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.political_state.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"372d8becf0f5a492a45b78f1c4bf95b2bcdd2729fe538ceef037f65c51451c22":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation/sense: community + rule","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation/sense: community + rule","exampleIds":[],"headword":"\u00e1pe\u00dbemvar\u00dfnen","id":"shakespeare014.lex.polity_state","ipa":"","label":"polity_state","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"\u00f4peshemvar\u014dnen","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"definition":"The governed political community, not merely someone\u2019s condition, and without imposing a modern nation-state or a particular constitution.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.polity_state.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"599e2c889ab544f193d21936ff87f86d27e77228d8acb12c3544cfab34b06da7":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-winters-tale.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"poliksenes","id":"shakespeare014.lex.polixenes_bohemian_king","ipa":"","label":"polixenes_bohemian_king","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"poliksenes","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-winters-tale.r1"}],"definition":"King of Bohemia, visiting the Sicilian court of his childhood friend.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.polixenes_bohemian_king.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"bcaebe14755b25f8799fe817a5d9bc16f1c8cea0e2e03b76a93fb6c21e42192d":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: defile + turn","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.loves-labors-lost.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: defile + turn","exampleIds":[],"headword":"murmayata\u00d9elyi\u00d1","id":"shakespeare014.lex.pollution_riddle_turn","ipa":"","label":"pollution_riddle_turn","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"murmayatangelyich","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.loves-labors-lost.r1"}],"definition":"Dull's second mistaken ending to the exchange. The recurring turn now begins with the root for defilement.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.pollution_riddle_turn.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"c8db8c551575603319c8ddffea9673de6c00a