 the wind and percussion instruments.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.psaltery_instrument.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"6e4f5d31935d9e4f7335d09a8cb6b42806f41e83b2cbe1b13030fc9004df81e2":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of ptolemy","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of ptolemy","exampleIds":[],"headword":"ptolemi","id":"shakespeare014.lex.ptolemaic_rulers","ipa":"","label":"ptolemaic_rulers","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"ptolemi","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"The dynastic plural Ptolemies in Cleopatra\u2019s request for her heirs\u2019 crown. Not a reference solely to Antony\u2019s child Ptolemy or a single earlier husband.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.ptolemaic_rulers.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"25a4cb68e2d2e1ea291495f7aad052db1fcebf0630e3fbdd27436e3734ddf885":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic adaptation of a personal or place name.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic adaptation of a personal or place name.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"ptolemi","id":"shakespeare014.lex.ptolemy","ipa":"","label":"ptolemy","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"ptolemi","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"Ptolemy as the royal name attached to Cleopatra\u2019s queenship and bed. Preserve the source\u2019s dynastic/marital designation without selecting an unprinted regnal number.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.ptolemy.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"af8714285e5cdbf8cc33ea8642ff1b054b915b0c0fd592e43e8ded455e0f5f60":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of ptolemy","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of ptolemy","exampleIds":[],"headword":"ptolemi","id":"shakespeare014.lex.ptolemy_antony_son","ipa":"","label":"ptolemy_antony_son","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"ptolemi","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"Antony\u2019s son Ptolemy, recipient of Syria, Cilicia and Phoenicia in Caesar\u2019s report. Distinct from the earlier Ptolemy in Cleopatra\u2019s queenship/bed reference despite the shared name.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.ptolemy_antony_son.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"87722ce422555b24e6f01dfb2e3ac1488aa01ecc30c1d5a705addf7a77906096":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation/sense: gather + people","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation/sense: gather + people","exampleIds":[],"headword":"z\u00dfgu\u00d9s\u00dflum","id":"shakespeare014.lex.public_assembly","ipa":"","label":"public_assembly","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"z\u014dgungs\u014dlum","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"definition":"An assembled public gathering, source congregations; not a specifically Christian congregation or an invented building.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.public_assembly.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"54bf0abce02a276f7c9f2458fb1912df14c9343eb5e1e6d250083fd7160fcbdb":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic adaptation of a personal or place name.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic adaptation of a personal or place name.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"publikola","id":"shakespeare014.lex.publicola_officer","ipa":"","label":"publicola_officer","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"publikola","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"Publicola in the list of commanders going to sea. A personal name, not an ordinary public-office label.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.publicola_officer.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"1a3040f9d6416c493ba76db3df4c5ee8bcbede4e8040f16ed9af88711da935c6":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"publikola","id":"shakespeare014.lex.publicola_valeria","ipa":"","label":"publicola_valeria","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"publikola","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"definition":"The Publicola identified here by his sister Valeria. This source supplies no identification with the naval officer in Antony and Cleopatra.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.publicola_valeria.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"56a3e9a81d69c04f736080eca368fac26228b2bbaebd5e39ced742b5d882844d":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native lexical derivation: proclaim","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native lexical derivation: proclaim","exampleIds":[],"headword":"olventondas\u00dflum","id":"shakespeare014.lex.publisher_revealer","ipa":"","label":"publisher_revealer","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"olventondas\u014dlum","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.lucrece.r1"}],"definition":"A person who makes something public, the publisher of a wife\u2019s beauty; not a modern printing business.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.publisher_revealer.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"67897a0270c79b986623c01008e743d848ccb99cb763edf97ef360a192a037cb":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"publius","id":"shakespeare014.lex.publius_ancestry","ipa":"","label":"publius_ancestry","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"publius","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"definition":"Publius of the Martian family in the source\u2019s water-conduit ancestry claim, distinct from other Publii in later plays. No invented surname prints.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.publius_ancestry.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"81e2a59784c12da91dc165bb67fa5bea48435ba3e10112745f9a604897d089ce":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.julius-caesar.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"publius","id":"shakespeare014.lex.publius_antony_nephew","ipa":"","label":"publius_antony_nephew","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"publius","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.julius-caesar.r1"}],"definition":"Antony's sister's son, marked for death in the proscription. His kinship distinguishes him from the exiled Cimber; the play does not identify him with the senator who greets Caesar.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.publius_antony_nephew.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"735d778716dd03785dacdf5cfb88f09bd9298f52b1954e8c6b160371dfaa79d0":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.julius-caesar.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"publius","id":"shakespeare014.lex.publius_cimber_exile","ipa":"","label":"publius_cimber_exile","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"publius","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.julius-caesar.r1"}],"definition":"The given name of Metellus Cimber's banished brother, distinct from the senator who attends Caesar.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.publius_cimber_exile.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"d3f58f3c9e63a4e3b8953f72cb923bed878a285ac6dd18b0ecaa42e1cd5c1d23":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.titus-andronicus.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"publius","id":"shakespeare014.lex.publius_marcus_son","ipa":"","label":"publius_marcus_son","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"publius","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.titus-andronicus.r1"}],"definition":"Marcus's son who joins the archers and later assists Titus.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.publius_marcus_son.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"695c3358b6b3ff27cefcf0ec91acfe592e01da9d278c70689905370c21614a30":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.julius-caesar.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"head