9s rare beloved; not merely statistically infrequent.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.rare_excellence.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"0bdd3615f26c5e5566d4630debf1afd77249b297fb6197b87b063abe60bd6c47":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of rare","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of rare","exampleIds":[],"headword":"vimp\u00e1l\u00dfn","id":"shakespeare014.lex.rarely_exceptional","ipa":"","label":"rarely_exceptional","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"adverb","pronunciation":"vimp\u00f4l\u014dn","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"Extraordinarily or to an exceptional degree, Cleopatra\u2019s rarely base insult. Contextual degree rather than how seldom the man behaves badly.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.rarely_exceptional.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"6a3ec13f13a0ddf6ec7e344736a70d1ae8a0c764e692233cf1b441080be61c69":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: rash","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.measure-for-measure.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: rash","exampleIds":[],"headword":"s\u00dfrnw\u00c5vumenmarin","id":"shakespeare014.lex.rash_prison_customer","ipa":"","label":"rash_prison_customer","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"s\u014drnw\u0101vumenmarin","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.measure-for-measure.r1"}],"definition":"The indebted customer who turned the paper and ginger into very little ready money.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.rash_prison_customer.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"dab463cc445149265f7e39bf05a0ff9916a97369e8bd857da5a35a86dd5f1671":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":