,"etymology":"Native lexical derivation from horse, ride","exampleIds":[],"headword":"thalthalven","id":"shakespeare014.lex.riding_horse","ipa":"","label":"riding_horse","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"thalthalven","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"definition":"A horse for riding, the palfrey addressed as the same animal as the courser; no new horse or asserted breed.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.riding_horse.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"d16a0d4370f92133c15e7995c0a9038652b09ae73828c57dda324ccf8b04b500":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of split","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of split","exampleIds":[],"headword":"stras","id":"shakespeare014.lex.rift_gap","ipa":"","label":"rift_gap","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"stras","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"The opening produced when the world cleaves in Octavia\u2019s imagined civil war. Nominal native split, not an unrelated named geographic feature.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.rift_gap.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"ccb15cae6c5452ce13c1702ba47193efa5020d848b64f4def0722beb99b94182":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation: secret + arrange","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation: secret + arrange","exampleIds":[],"headword":"o\u00c3brenhif\u00e5ror","id":"shakespeare014.lex.rig_card_game","ipa":"","label":"rig_card_game","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"ojzhbrenhifouror","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"Secretly arrange cards to cheat, Antony\u2019s accusation that Cleopatra and Caesar packed cards. Native secret-arrange, not packing luggage.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.rig_card_game.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"6cf72146f7ff396b9aa97bd285cc8ada82113eb7173d06cb57955e65ddddfd07":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of kjv_rigging","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of kjv_rigging","exampleIds":[],"headword":"meranthiril jw\u00ebnenplesten","id":"shakespeare014.lex.rig_vessel","ipa":"","label":"rig_vessel","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"meranthiril jw\u00fcnenplesten","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"Equip vessels with their necessary rigging for the fleet\u2019s departure. Explicit action from native ship-cord; no fabricated rig plan or modern vessel type.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.rig_vessel.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"1e3cafdace68763f8f7c7992270bf5709f837b3a1cf13ab0ff07c49562f41a1c":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_right_side","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_right_side","exampleIds":[],"headword":"luren","id":"shakespeare014.lex.right_side","ipa":"","label":"right_side","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"luren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"definition":"Anatomical right-hand direction, distinct from just entitlement.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.right_side.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"0350db2aa11435