ively found in stones by the Duke; native teach + speech, with no literal new preacher in the forest.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.sermon_teaching.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"12f0af8d14bdc64a8454e2a17762c54efa0843b2e7e7b0c96d087909a4cec0ae":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: skin + sickness","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.measure-for-measure.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: skin + sickness","exampleIds":[],"headword":"shalemmuren","id":"shakespeare014.lex.serpigo_skin_affliction","ipa":"","label":"serpigo_skin_affliction","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"shalemmuren","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.measure-for-measure.r1"}],"definition":"A spreading skin eruption in the disguised duke's list of afflictions; the species of disease is not specified.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.serpigo_skin_affliction.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"5323e41309bb18f78c7f25179db8a5fbd29abaa1058e6521690b3b82b7d8c407":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of servant","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of servant","exampleIds":[],"headword":"d\u00c7v","id":"shakespeare014.lex.servant_labourer","ipa":"","label":"servant_labourer","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"d\u00e3v","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"definition":"A household or estate worker with whom Orlando is made to feed, source hind; never the female deer.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.servant_labourer.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"beed5144c704a1044fc9fffd8b7f2b408b3fe2dcd9acac2f9863c2686a620f66":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native deriva