are014.lex.shilling_source.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"bdc5acaa74666bd18f13391d5b43b8a3d8a9026439bdf9910454335644db71ea":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native compound: leg + bone","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native compound: leg + bone","exampleIds":[],"headword":"palkran","id":"shakespeare014.lex.shin_body","ipa":"","label":"shin_body","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"palkran","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.as-you-like-it.r1"}],"definition":"The front bony part of the lower leg struck in Touchstone\u2019s wit metaphor. Native leg + bone lexicalization names this region without asserting that every leg bone is a shin.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.shin_body.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"ca36bd861ee9938c40b8494b4978f2358f89bf15d178bf77a6d0d0258e38596f":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation: ship + chamber","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation: ship + chamber","exampleIds":[],"headword":"merankinem","id":"shakespeare014.lex.ship_cabin","ipa":"","label":"ship_cabin","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"merankinem","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"The private room aboard the vessel to which Menas invites Enobarbus. Native ship-room; no extra cabin plan or land cottage supplied.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.ship_cabin.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"1a8e917673e156ffb815ca6888b5e36f2abca9f16590cb6d3d70540c4a0399c3":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: deck_surface + door","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-tempest.r1"}],"etymology"