ress.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"9b80e983dae7ae4069ad2f665bfbc260d4701f121b2dbbb104d3a68c139e14d5":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: break + cake","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-merry-wives-of-windsor.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: break + cake","exampleIds":[],"headword":"ika\u00d9pelam","id":"shakespeare014.lex.shortcake_book_borrower","ipa":"","label":"shortcake_book_borrower","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"ikangpelam","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-merry-wives-of-windsor.r1"}],"definition":"Alice's edible surname, a cake which breaks easily. Distinct from the Messina watchman's Oatcake.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.shortcake_book_borrower.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"24d5c614db3f7bd7efba0ad6eff7eac5179bb52917bcfb3fbdda53beb6f2e6c1":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_shoulder","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_shoulder","exampleIds":[],"headword":"larnaorthrenin","id":"shakespeare014.lex.shoulder","ipa":"","label":"shoulder","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"larnaorthrenin","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"definition":"The upper junction of arm and body, here the shoulder over which Venus lowers her head.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.shoulder.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"7ced3658e4382a42690492c2328e45c2285cc6507e3c7175a0b8fd5ec997fccb":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: plank_board + silver_coin","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-merry-wives-of-windsor.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: plank_board + silver_coin","exampleIds":[],"headword":"y\u00eblshalinve\u00dbzarzarven","id":"shakespeare014.lex.shovelboard_game_coin","ipa":"","label":"shovelboard_game_coin","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"y\u00fclshalinveshzarzarven","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-merry-wives-of-windsor.r1"}],"definition":"A silver piece slid across a board in the game. Slender describes two Edward pieces he bought above their face value.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.shovelboard_game_coin.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"1f9f6e0760303dbe50397d69eae6788522c362a3a7ae5d0efd93b4473f71f534":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation: show + ground","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation: show + ground","exampleIds":[],"headword":"gl\u00c9stjo\u00d9","id":"shakespeare014.lex.showplace_arena","ipa":"","label":"showplace_arena","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"gl\u00e4stjong","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"The public area for performances or exercise in Caesar\u2019s account. Native show-ground, without imposing a particular amphitheatre plan.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.showplace_arena.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"2d65ff9e85fb21afe8575c6b62e5ae9fd7a0698ae0fc69a996ac228296fd4d03":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation: show + clothing","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation: show + clothing","exampleIds":[],"headword":"gl\u00c9stvelvor","id":"shakespeare014.lex.showy_trappings","ipa":"","label":"showy_trappings","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciat