ed in Petruchio's comparison of ill-tempered wives.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.socrates_athenian.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"9cb2cd92fd6820b6ec96d713c04839a8dff7912a35103864f8c60f32bf9ed9d7":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.troilus-and-cressida.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"sol","id":"shakespeare014.lex.sol_planetary_sun","ipa":"","label":"sol_planetary_sun","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"sol","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.troilus-and-cressida.r1"}],"definition":"The sun named in Ulysses's comparison between planetary and political rank.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.sol_planetary_sun.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"b22b70b6f27b8f87d6ac5487584d9f659e3f648311a48514ecd7119d4878bc91":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Source-specific musical syllable paired with the established fa.","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-taming-of-the-shrew.r1"}],"etymology":"Source-specific musical syllable paired with the established fa.","exampleIds":[],"headword":"s\u00dfl","id":"shakespeare014.lex.sol_solmization_syllable","ipa":"","label":"sol_solmization_syllable","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"citation","pronunciation":"s\u014dl","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-taming-of-the-shrew.r1"}],"definition":"The sung syllable sol in Petruchio's threat and Hortensio's lesson.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.sol_solmization_syllable.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"a1408a007a8bbb58770c7e6304895c6e8a7037130c7187d79c948769cb0d6d74":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-merchant-of-venice.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"solanyo","id":"shakespeare014.lex.solanio_antonio_friend","ipa":"","label":"solanio_antonio_friend","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"solanyo","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-merchant-of-venice.r1"}],"definition":"Antonio's interlocutor who conjures up the wind and maps. Distinct from Salarino and Salerio.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.solanio_antonio_friend.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"bf52e5aeb541cad395afee235f8cbcae5fd9e861d6978011c8aaa24846a491e5":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of kjv_solder","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of kjv_solder","exampleIds":[],"headword":"zarkl\u00e1r","id":"shakespeare014.lex.solder_join","ipa":"","label":"solder_join","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"zarkl\u00f4r","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"Join the rift in Octavia\u2019s imagined divided world with slain bodies as the joining substance. Native metal-join metaphor retained without importing an idol-making scene or asserting a real repair.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.solder_join.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"ed95d6a1d86d3c9e4a20871fd0faae9449ad854e2c0aa6b993ec2f1b865ff97b":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of staff","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of staff","exampleIds":[],"headword":"teral","id":"shakespeare014.lex.soldier_rally_pole","ipa":"","label":"soldier_rally_pole","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"teral","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"The soldier\u2019s elevated pole or central point of reference, the image of Antony falling. Preserve the pole image and military rallying force without claiming the disputed image can only mean the North Star or a particular festival pole.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.soldier_rally_pole.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"6b64dd43c1daca380095d1c4894ea8e36fba9d1c8b4cbb9b63f2f3c19f7d8091":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: shoe + bottom","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.julius-caesar.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: shoe + bottom","exampleIds":[],"headword":"palindur\u00ebn","id":"shakespeare014.lex.sole_shoe_underpart","ipa":"","label":"sole_shoe_underpart","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"palindur\u00fcn","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.julius-caesar.r1"}],"definition":"The lower working surface of a shoe, in the cobbler's play on the source words soles and souls.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.sole_shoe_underpart.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"3818bec036bb065499ca994f55f04cc827dba88aaf861dcf6bbaa3a769a1b168":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: coin_currency + piece","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.timon-of-athens.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: coin_currency + piece","exampleIds":[],"headword":"zarzarventhrenin","id":"shakespeare014.lex.solidare_athenian_coin","ipa":"","label":"solidare_athenian_coin","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"zarzarventhrenin","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.timon-of-athens.r1"}],"definition":"The coin Lucullus offers Flaminius for concealing their encounter. No exchange rate or metal is asserted.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.solidare_athenian_coin.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"9a59fc4612e22cb35d8ca5b2f41437a460ca543857c004032635df667a7f328f":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-comedy-of-errors.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"solinus","id":"shakespeare014.lex.solinus_ephesus_duke","ipa":"","label":"solinus_ephesus_duke","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"solinus","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-comedy-of-errors.r1"}],"definition":"Duke of Ephesus, who sentences Egeon and later witnesses the reunion.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.solinus_ephesus_duke.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"131ac60e3dae18867d064dc3c7e23c03d26ce36fdc9fbe579b912eb416a6c61b":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.titus-andronicus.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"solon","id":"shakespeare014.lex.solon_athenian_lawgiver","ipa":"","label":"solon_athenian_lawgiver","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"solon","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.titus-andronicus.r1"}],"definition":"The Athenian lawgiver invoked by Marcus while contrasting living success with honor secure at death.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.solon_athenian_lawgiver.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"9d226fe7fd09cf81e1498d071529ed7dd347be24b9788836e4ad04b3ed65af17":{"au