pe.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"fca8a5a9a65ab47904e6406a58217462203171441d8caeca4f80ce69e709670e":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of kjv_rudder_acts","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense/identity of kjv_rudder_acts","exampleIds":[],"headword":"meranelyi\u00d1","id":"shakespeare014.lex.steer_course","ipa":"","label":"steer_course","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"verb","pronunciation":"meranelyich","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.antony-and-cleopatra.r1"}],"definition":"Direct a vessel\u2019s course, native ship-turn used as an action. The attendant steers; no Acts voyage or shipwreck is imported.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.steer_course.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"12a5fa460e2fae379fb0d9a1dddbbdfaa971a641a84a00d7627eb994f207d93b":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-tempest.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","exampleIds":[],"headword":"stefano","id":"shakespeare014.lex.stephano_alonso_butler","ipa":"","label":"stephano_alonso_butler","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"proper","pronunciation":"stefano","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-tempest.r1"}],"definition":"Alonso's butler, distinct from the servant in Belmont.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.stephano_alonso_butler.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"e639ae1188ef127b44e7c7412ab23f1383917b9ef8f31e11cbab074878387b20":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptation","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.the-merchant-of-venice.r1"}],"etymology":"Author-permitted phonetic personal-name adaptat