ing against the door in the poem\u2019s personified warning.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.threshold.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"b9dbdf50798d91d32b9c7026d1fd52a9e925c18c0bcf0033be48e4ecd315b5e7":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation or sense: spare + expense","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.hamlet.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation or sense: spare + expense","exampleIds":[],"headword":"jem\u00e3ma\u00e5vbebis","id":"shakespeare014.lex.thrift_household","ipa":"","label":"thrift_household","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"jemoimaouvbebis","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.hamlet.r1"}],"definition":"Economy in household spending. Hamlet repeats it bitterly of serving funeral meats at the wedding.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.thrift_household.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"6ef861bd351c48071a4043802170338f0daf1e11096e8a83f68be33d8f9b79f4":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_throat","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed contextual sense of kjv_throat","exampleIds":[],"headword":"tommarjo\u00d9","id":"shakespeare014.lex.throat","ipa":"","label":"throat","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"tommarjong","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"definition":"Throat or gullet, here the eagle\u2019s gorge receiving prey.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.throat.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"8a3ad606d7b975aac53f91db7a9fe434fd3663d287ee4ce0e4da3a0e27244c5f":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation/sense: kjv_thumb","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation/sense: kjv_thumb","exampleI