y of Antony\u2019s sadness or mirth, which Cleopatra finds becoming; not an added act of physical assault.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.violence_intensity.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"5c260b3465903dbd8cff344330a833dc41c050256588b0060edbdd6f8341caac":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Reviewed literary sense of violet","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"etymology":"Reviewed literary sense of violet","exampleIds":[],"headword":"ed\u00df","id":"shakespeare014.lex.violet_flower","ipa":"","label":"violet_flower","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"ed\u014d","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.venus-and-adonis.r1"}],"definition":"The violet flower, a lexical botanical sense of the author-attested colour root, not just the colour adjective.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.violet_flower.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"f327cc2054e528068ef5551f2d7e130f0fd1c8fd584647fba215d0cc0a957b2c":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Authored native derivation/sense: kjv_viper","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"etymology":"Authored native derivation/sense: kjv_viper","exampleIds":[],"headword":"murnamsilvar","id":"shakespeare014.lex.viper_serpent","ipa":"","label":"viper_serpent","notes":"","orthographyId":"thimfora-79","partOfSpeech":"noun","pronunciation":"murnamsilvar","senses":[{"citations":[{"locator":"Authored lexical decision","sourceId":"shakespeare014.source.coriolanus.r1"}],"definition":"A venomous snake in Sicinius\u2019s accusation against Coriolanus. Reviewed native poison-serpent; no actual transformation or modern species identification is asserted.","id":"shakespeare014.lex.viper_serpent.sense","status":"draft"}],"status":"draft","variants":[]},"ae4afa9574f78a58a134a7211fad02dfbbabb698fe7475f1dee00bd391fe6b02":{"audioLinks":[],"citations":[{"locator":"Author-permitted ph